WEBVTT

00:36.136 --> 00:38.343
SHOWBOX presents

00:40.042 --> 00:42.248
a SHOWBOX, PINETOWN PRODUCTION production

00:45.895 --> 00:48.749
EXHUMA

01:00.942 --> 01:03.972
Miss, we will be landing soon.

01:03.973 --> 01:06.222
Would you like some more wine?

01:07.202 --> 01:08.992
No, I'm all right.

01:09.692 --> 01:11.632
And just so you know...

01:11.633 --> 01:12.982
I'm Korean.

01:13.032 --> 01:15.582
I understand. I apologize.

01:15.602 --> 01:17.032
Have a pleasant flight.

01:32.212 --> 01:34.840
Our representative...

01:34.903 --> 01:38.302
Well, his main business is real estate.

01:38.441 --> 01:40.298
He owns quite a lot of land in Korea,

01:40.299 --> 01:43.522
and he also does investment business
across various places in the US.

01:43.599 --> 01:45.475
Well, you know the sort of
people I'm talking about.

01:45.549 --> 01:47.519
People who were born rich.

01:47.604 --> 01:50.314
Exorbitantly rich people.

01:53.502 --> 01:55.672
How am I supposed to trust them?

01:55.752 --> 01:58.002
You should have considered my opinion, too.

01:58.472 --> 02:01.472
These are totally different circumstances.

02:01.962 --> 02:04.482
I don't get it. Just do whatever you want.

02:16.881 --> 02:20.761
He's calmed down now
because of the medication,

02:20.831 --> 02:23.639
but he hasn't stopped crying
since he was born.

02:24.310 --> 02:27.466
The renowned medical staff
has tried everything,

02:27.467 --> 02:30.437
but they say there's nothing wrong
from a medical point of view.

02:31.518 --> 02:33.398
We've already been informed.

02:40.405 --> 02:43.713
Excuse me, could you leave us
alone in the room, please?

02:43.807 --> 02:44.952
Excuse me?

02:50.832 --> 02:54.132
 By the words of the Heavenly Venerable,
I summon the 9 inner spirits: 

02:54.133 --> 02:56.433
 the celestial birth, the spirit
of absence, the mysterious pearl, 

02:56.434 --> 02:58.632
 the central righteousness, the cinnabar
elixir, the spirit of cyclic change, 

02:58.633 --> 03:00.802
 the elixir of the source of life,
the great abyss and the spirit of youth. 

03:00.803 --> 03:02.103
 I call upon the 3 core essences: 

03:02.104 --> 03:04.673
 the great brightness, the invigorating spirit
and the imperturbable essence. 

03:04.674 --> 03:06.904
 When the 5 yin organs are disturbed,
when the 6 meridians are shaken, 

03:06.905 --> 03:11.105
 when the limbs lose their harmony, when
the joints are in distress, recite this scripture. 

03:24.866 --> 03:27.411
There must be other family members
suffering from the same illness.

03:27.481 --> 03:29.121
The baby's father...

03:30.080 --> 03:32.023
And the baby's grandfather.

03:39.339 --> 03:41.592
Is she talking about my husband
and my father-in-law?

03:41.592 --> 03:43.510
 The expressions on their faces... 

03:43.510 --> 03:44.261
Yes.

03:44.261 --> 03:48.948
 How they've changed from
suspicion to astonishment... 

03:52.180 --> 03:57.011
 People always live in bright places,
and only look towards radiant ones. 

03:57.012 --> 03:59.609
CHAPTER I: YIN-YANG
AND THE FIVE ELEMENTS

03:59.610 --> 04:01.737
 The world must be bathed in bright light 

04:01.737 --> 04:03.697
 for it to be visible to our eyes.

04:04.239 --> 04:05.574
 And people... 

04:05.575 --> 04:09.119
 They believe only in the
things they can see and touch. 

04:12.122 --> 04:14.458
 A world bathed in bright light... 

04:16.335 --> 04:19.004
 And what lies beyond it. 

04:25.249 --> 04:29.723
 People have known about those
dark beings since ancient times. 

04:30.220 --> 04:32.472
 They've given them various names. 

04:32.976 --> 04:37.189
 Ghosts, devils, goblins, monsters... 

04:37.481 --> 04:41.610
 They ceaselessly yearn for
bright places, harboring envy, 

04:41.944 --> 04:43.778
 so from time to time, 

04:43.779 --> 04:46.323
 they resort to tricks to cross over. 

04:49.177 --> 04:52.287
 And when that happens,
people come to me. 

04:55.958 --> 04:57.959
 In between yin and yang, 

04:57.960 --> 05:00.461
 in between science and superstition, 

05:00.462 --> 05:03.422
 the people who find themselves
right in between these contrasts. 

05:03.423 --> 05:06.343
 I am Lee Hwarim, a shaman. 

05:06.459 --> 05:08.679
I received word from my wife.

05:08.750 --> 05:10.222
I'm Park Ji-yong.

05:20.864 --> 05:22.025
My older brother...

05:22.484 --> 05:25.070
He ended up committing suicide
in a mental hospital.

05:25.570 --> 05:27.281
Since then, I...

05:27.698 --> 05:29.049
As well as...

05:30.409 --> 05:33.078
...my newborn son, we've
been going through this.

05:33.704 --> 05:37.749
When I close my eyes,
someone screams.

05:38.542 --> 05:39.668
And chokes me.

05:41.169 --> 05:44.673
It's something the eldest
grandchildren experience.

05:45.674 --> 05:48.135
At first they usually suspect
a hereditary disease.

05:48.135 --> 05:51.513
Later on they suspect issues with the
house foundation and decide to move.

05:51.513 --> 05:53.348
The shadow.

05:53.473 --> 05:56.059
As soon as I walked in, I
noticed a shadow in this house.

05:56.476 --> 05:59.029
The shadow of one of your ancestors.

06:00.147 --> 06:03.692
It's most likely the shadow of your grandfather.

06:04.192 --> 06:05.199
My grandfather?

06:05.260 --> 06:07.331
Simply put, it's deterioration of the grave.

06:07.332 --> 06:10.948
It's usually referred to as a
misfortune related to the grave.

06:10.949 --> 06:13.177
In other words, one of your ancestors

06:13.178 --> 06:15.370
is complaining about the discomfort
he's experiencing.

06:16.496 --> 06:17.497
Are you sure?

06:17.498 --> 06:18.498
Yes.

06:18.832 --> 06:20.058
One hundred percent.

06:22.461 --> 06:23.462
Then...

06:23.962 --> 06:26.298
What should I do?

06:28.133 --> 06:30.093
You need to spend money and hire people.

06:30.190 --> 06:31.803
I can't do it on my own.

06:31.853 --> 06:34.389
We need to call in experts...

06:35.349 --> 06:37.476
Damn it...

06:38.226 --> 06:41.104
Their creepy faces already come to mind...

07:08.674 --> 07:09.925
The grave has been opened!

07:10.004 --> 07:11.510
The grave has been opened!

07:15.222 --> 07:17.683
The deceased is waking up, stop staring.

07:17.683 --> 07:18.976
Oh, we're sorry.

07:18.976 --> 07:21.096
Let's go.

07:21.187 --> 07:21.770
Come on, quickly.

07:23.522 --> 07:25.816
One, two, three!

07:35.701 --> 07:37.703
The water hasn't seeped in.

07:38.412 --> 07:42.026
We apologize for waking you up.

07:43.083 --> 07:44.418
Well, it's clean.

07:44.472 --> 07:47.296
And fragrant.

07:47.383 --> 07:49.840
Why did they put so much stuff in here?

07:51.091 --> 07:52.718
All these...

07:52.718 --> 07:54.303
Unbelievable.

07:54.303 --> 07:57.028
I keep telling people not to
put metal objects inside.

07:57.029 --> 07:59.034
Causing discomfort to the deceased...

08:00.726 --> 08:02.102
Director Kim.

08:02.102 --> 08:05.022
Your mother and all your
family elders resting here,

08:05.023 --> 08:07.149
I've taken care of all of them, right?

08:07.215 --> 08:09.067
Yes, you sure did.

08:09.143 --> 08:14.072
And I assume everyone's healthy
and business is thriving.

08:14.072 --> 08:15.741
Yes, all thanks to you.

08:15.741 --> 08:19.661
Even if I dig up this place again...

08:19.743 --> 08:24.667
This is one of the most auspicious burial sites
I've found in my 40-year career, you know that?

08:24.708 --> 08:27.461
Look, the Five Elements
are in perfect harmony.

08:27.534 --> 08:29.212
I'm telling you.

08:29.880 --> 08:31.590
And I gave it to you cheap.

08:31.590 --> 08:32.799
Damn it.

08:32.799 --> 08:34.301
That's true...

08:35.093 --> 08:37.387
So don't worry.

08:37.804 --> 08:40.432
You're doing the right thing reburying her.

08:40.849 --> 08:43.726
If you say it, then it must be so.

08:43.727 --> 08:44.960
But...

08:44.961 --> 08:47.272
Why does she keep appearing
in my children's dreams?

08:47.273 --> 08:49.858
Lately, even my wife says she
sees her mother in her dreams.

08:50.734 --> 08:51.902
Mortician Go!

08:52.527 --> 08:54.071
Still not done?

08:54.180 --> 08:55.485
Hey, I'm hungry.

08:55.552 --> 08:58.659
So am I, and so is this person.

08:58.731 --> 09:01.453
The one in charge of the shrouding
didn't check, did he?

09:01.524 --> 09:02.704
- Do the numbers match?
- Yes.

09:02.704 --> 09:04.539
Very well.

09:18.503 --> 09:20.988
Someone has taken Grandma's dentures.

09:23.225 --> 09:26.335
I said someone is in possession
of Grandma's dentures.

09:37.364 --> 09:38.782
Did you...

09:39.449 --> 09:41.450
Did you take Grandma's dentures?

09:41.451 --> 09:42.759
Sang-hyun, you...

09:42.760 --> 09:44.348
That thing in your closet...

09:44.349 --> 09:45.622
Those were Grandma's dentures?!

09:45.622 --> 09:48.010
But why would you...

09:48.011 --> 09:50.335
All of Grandma's things were burned...

09:51.086 --> 09:53.038
Now that Grandma's gone...

09:53.880 --> 09:55.299
Dad...

09:55.300 --> 09:57.551
I had to keep something...

09:57.552 --> 09:59.094
Little buddy!

09:59.095 --> 10:01.555
Grandma says she's hungry,
you need to return them to her.

10:01.556 --> 10:03.390
If I do...

10:03.391 --> 10:06.226
Then how will I remember Grandma?

10:06.227 --> 10:08.577
I don't have anything else
that belonged to her.

10:08.578 --> 10:10.355
Did you say your name's Sang-hyun?

10:10.416 --> 10:11.648
Sang-hyun...

10:12.190 --> 10:14.358
Your Grandma...

10:14.359 --> 10:16.111
...is always by your side.

10:24.703 --> 10:25.887
 Blood ties. 

10:27.039 --> 10:29.491
 They bind us, even beyond death. 

10:29.492 --> 10:31.509
- Sis...
 - When individuals have common genes, 

10:31.510 --> 10:33.795
 they share a common
body and a collective mind. 

10:35.047 --> 10:39.301
 When the human body ends its activities,
it becomes dust and earth. 

10:40.135 --> 10:44.181
 And we inhale that dust,
and tread on that earth. 

10:44.181 --> 10:46.767
 Living, dying, and being reborn. 

10:46.767 --> 10:48.977
 A cycle that repeats endlessly. 

10:49.043 --> 10:50.228
 In other words, 

10:50.228 --> 10:54.650
 the earth connects us and
makes everything circulate. 

10:55.108 --> 10:58.820
 Those who call it superstition
or fraud, screw them all! 

10:58.895 --> 11:01.333
 Because for the select 1%
who represent Korea's elite, 

11:01.334 --> 11:03.733
 feng shui means both religion and science. 

11:05.786 --> 11:08.021
 I'm a geomancer. 

11:08.038 --> 11:12.119
 I find and dig up lands for both
the living and the dead. 

11:12.120 --> 11:15.044
 My name is Kim Sang-deok
and I'm a feng shui expert. 

11:16.421 --> 11:18.924
 A survey has revealed
that many domestic companies 

11:18.925 --> 11:23.053
 perceive the current economic
situation as a long-term recession. 

11:23.054 --> 11:24.471
 According to the survey, Korea... 

11:24.514 --> 11:26.640
Wait until it's cooked!

11:28.129 --> 11:29.599
Why should I wait for it?

11:29.600 --> 11:31.420
When it starts sizzling, it's just right.

11:31.645 --> 11:33.605
To be honest, that place
we stopped by today...

11:33.606 --> 11:35.023
That place...

11:35.023 --> 11:38.360
- Is it really an auspicious burial site?
- What in the world...

11:38.360 --> 11:40.529
What are you saying?
He's a regular client, after all.

11:40.645 --> 11:43.073
But seeing that grave...

11:43.166 --> 11:45.659
Well, the Black Tortoise up north
looked kind of ambiguous,

11:45.659 --> 11:48.659
and the shape of the White
Tiger out west was...

11:48.660 --> 11:49.287
I'm not really sure.

11:49.288 --> 11:52.082
You think you're a feng shui expert now?

11:52.174 --> 11:53.917
If you're so knowledgeable,

11:53.996 --> 11:56.012
go ahead and do it
on your own from now on.

11:56.013 --> 11:57.796
I've been thinking about something.

11:57.897 --> 12:02.009
In Korea, an average of 250,000
people die annually,

12:02.009 --> 12:04.076
of which 30% are buried.

12:04.077 --> 12:08.140
So starting from the Joseon dynasty,
in these narrow lands,

12:08.140 --> 12:11.059
in every good spot, plenty of people
have already been buried.

12:11.060 --> 12:15.564
So claiming that there are still
auspicious burial sites out there is...

12:15.628 --> 12:18.025
- It's a bit...
- Well...

12:18.817 --> 12:20.902
I'd give that burial site 65 points.

12:20.903 --> 12:22.849
So not one hundred.

12:22.942 --> 12:25.407
Now the seeds have dried,
they're long gone.

12:25.949 --> 12:28.619
Listen, all the funeral directors like yourself

12:28.619 --> 12:30.662
are working for funeral service companies,

12:30.663 --> 12:33.498
while geomancers like me
who make a living digging up the earth,

12:33.499 --> 12:35.417
they all end up working
on construction sites.

12:35.418 --> 12:37.044
It's the final lap!

12:37.093 --> 12:39.129
We are the last survivors.

12:39.129 --> 12:41.298
- I'll pour you a drink.
- Hold on.

12:41.298 --> 12:42.591
Did they arrive this quickly?

12:42.591 --> 12:44.301
Oh my, you're early.

12:44.301 --> 12:45.677
Hey, it's been a while.

12:45.677 --> 12:46.929
- Hi.
- Hey.

12:46.929 --> 12:47.930
- Come in.
- Sure.

12:47.930 --> 12:49.181
Oh, my!

12:49.252 --> 12:51.642
The scent of pine mushrooms
has reached Seoul.

12:51.642 --> 12:53.769
- I must bear with it.
- He already ate them all.

12:53.769 --> 12:55.646
What are you saying?

12:55.705 --> 12:57.356
- How have you been?
- Welcome back.

12:57.356 --> 12:58.774
I should have contacted you more often.

12:58.774 --> 13:00.400
It's all right, you're a busy man.

13:00.400 --> 13:01.485
But...

13:01.485 --> 13:03.111
Bong-gil has gotten even more handsome!

13:03.111 --> 13:04.154
Oh, really?

13:04.154 --> 13:05.614
That's right.

13:05.614 --> 13:07.616
The girls always take him for walks.

13:07.617 --> 13:08.992
It's becoming a bad habit.

13:08.993 --> 13:10.619
How long has it been?

13:10.619 --> 13:12.579
- About 3 years?
- Yes.

13:12.579 --> 13:13.789
Time flies.

13:14.289 --> 13:15.040
So...

13:15.093 --> 13:16.833
How's business going these days?

13:16.833 --> 13:18.585
So-so.

13:18.639 --> 13:21.363
- It's off-season now.
- So here I am,

13:21.364 --> 13:23.966
- visiting the elders again...
- Wait a minute.

13:23.966 --> 13:26.593
I smell something.

13:26.593 --> 13:28.095
Don't you smell anything?

13:28.095 --> 13:30.681
What kind of smell?
The smell of money?

13:30.713 --> 13:33.183
Yeah, I think that's what it smells like.

13:33.242 --> 13:35.269
Damn it...

13:35.269 --> 13:37.521
I tried to hide it, but...

13:38.438 --> 13:39.356
You got me.

13:41.873 --> 13:43.485
Come on, spill the beans.

13:43.485 --> 13:46.571
How did he catch on so fast?

13:52.265 --> 13:54.037
After a trusted doctor introduced them to me,

13:54.038 --> 13:57.207
I visited a strange family living in the US.

13:57.541 --> 13:59.459
Someone named Park Ji-yong.

13:59.459 --> 14:02.045
His family lineage is Korean up to his father,

14:02.046 --> 14:04.548
but from him onward, they
have American nationality.

14:04.840 --> 14:06.216
Simply put, he's...

14:06.217 --> 14:07.884
Rich, filthy rich.

14:08.343 --> 14:09.595
That's a good start!

14:10.887 --> 14:13.307
The eldest grandchildren
suffer from spiritual illnesses.

14:13.307 --> 14:14.391
Even a newborn.

14:14.391 --> 14:16.018
Oh, boy...

14:16.018 --> 14:17.936
He endured it for quite a while.

14:18.604 --> 14:19.980
Isn't it possession?

14:19.980 --> 14:22.357
Hasn't reached that point yet.

14:23.191 --> 14:24.818
From what I've seen...

14:24.818 --> 14:27.696
It's deterioration of the grave.

14:29.782 --> 14:34.482
Are you really gonna dig up
your grandfather's grave?

14:36.062 --> 14:38.852
It's been almost one hundred years.

14:39.322 --> 14:41.222
I don't need your approval.

14:41.362 --> 14:43.272
I've made up my mind.

14:45.622 --> 14:48.962
You really believe in such things?

14:49.152 --> 14:53.092
And you think your aunt
in Korea will agree on this?

14:56.242 --> 14:58.132
I'm the head of the family.

14:59.062 --> 15:00.792
So I make the decisions.

15:02.766 --> 15:06.109
First of all, I don't trust those people.

15:06.735 --> 15:09.196
If something goes wrong,
things will only get worse.

15:09.571 --> 15:11.448
The baby will get better soon.

15:13.450 --> 15:15.535
Let's pray together,

15:16.235 --> 15:18.330
and continue the treatment.

15:30.092 --> 15:31.635
We just...

15:31.635 --> 15:35.180
All we need to do is live
quietly and away from it all.

15:55.075 --> 15:58.453
Why would it matter if her belly
shows during the wedding?

15:58.454 --> 16:00.322
There's no better dowry than that!

16:00.323 --> 16:02.457
But still. Me having a grandson?

16:02.458 --> 16:04.109
Not to mention that
he'll have blonde hair.

16:04.110 --> 16:06.712
And his blue eyes will
glow like headlights!

16:06.712 --> 16:08.213
What an outdated mindset.

16:08.214 --> 16:11.133
But will Yeon-hee continue living
in Germany after getting married?

16:11.134 --> 16:14.386
What are you talking about?
She has to live in Korea.

16:14.527 --> 16:16.096
Speaking of which...

16:16.305 --> 16:20.767
I was somewhat worried about money,
given Yeon-hee's marriage,

16:20.767 --> 16:23.478
- but we've landed a major catch this time.
- That's right.

16:23.478 --> 16:25.105
Our Savior,

16:25.105 --> 16:29.693
he even takes care of my
pension at the right moment.

16:29.757 --> 16:30.694
Amen!

16:32.359 --> 16:35.216
But how rich is this guy,

16:35.217 --> 16:37.826
that he's paying us 500 million won each
to relocate the grave?

16:37.912 --> 16:40.078
You think that's all?
He likely paid more.

16:40.078 --> 16:41.288
What? More?

16:41.288 --> 16:44.791
You know how cunning Hwarim is.

16:44.791 --> 16:46.418
You think she didn't secure
a little extra for herself?

16:46.470 --> 16:48.003
That's true.

16:48.072 --> 16:51.590
She seems naive but she's not.

16:56.428 --> 17:00.223
First of all, I'd like you to tell me
your grandfather's name and his hometown.

17:00.682 --> 17:06.772
Typically I inquire about the reputation
of the family members as well as their jobs,

17:06.772 --> 17:09.062
but since you said it's urgent...

17:09.149 --> 17:14.279
Shouldn't the person receiving the money
be the one to prove he's trustworthy?

17:17.032 --> 17:18.492
Oh...

17:18.867 --> 17:20.494
Trust?

17:21.203 --> 17:22.454
Fine, then.

17:22.585 --> 17:25.666
If you don't want to do this,
let's just forget about the whole thing.

17:25.736 --> 17:28.126
Would you please follow just two things?

17:28.752 --> 17:31.463
Please ensure that today's events remain private.

17:31.838 --> 17:34.508
And please carry out the cremation right away.

17:35.968 --> 17:38.730
With the coffin intact.

17:38.731 --> 17:40.221
Intact?

17:40.222 --> 17:42.431
You're saying not to open it at all?

17:42.432 --> 17:44.059
Does it make any difference?

17:44.810 --> 17:46.478
Even if you relocate it,

17:46.478 --> 17:48.438
it still ends up being cremated anyhow.

17:48.438 --> 17:50.440
Listen to me.

17:50.440 --> 17:53.610
Usually this needs to be reported
to the district office first.

17:53.704 --> 17:57.489
After the coffin is opened, the
funeral director gathers the remains,

17:57.489 --> 18:01.034
then it needs to be moved
to another location to be cremated.

18:01.326 --> 18:02.452
Do you understand?

18:06.873 --> 18:08.458
Anyway, for now...

18:09.042 --> 18:10.586
Let's see the burial site first.

18:10.623 --> 18:13.964
My parents and the other relatives
are quite against it,

18:14.060 --> 18:15.360
so I'd like to get it over with
as soon as possible...

18:15.361 --> 18:18.071
I said let's see the burial site first.

18:18.072 --> 18:23.026
CHAPTER II: UNNAMED GRAVE

18:23.027 --> 18:25.434
It's in the northern part of Gangwon Province...

18:25.498 --> 18:27.728
That's rather unsettling.

18:27.788 --> 18:29.980
But the fact that we can't open the coffin,

18:29.980 --> 18:31.982
that's pretty strange.

18:31.982 --> 18:34.860
Shouldn't we be checking the remains?

18:35.152 --> 18:38.737
This means the shrouding
is out of the question.

18:39.197 --> 18:41.825
Could there be something in the coffin?

18:42.402 --> 18:44.902
BOGUKSA TEMPLE

20:31.101 --> 20:33.729
Have you ever seen a grave on top of a mountain?

20:34.021 --> 20:35.314
It's uncommon.

20:36.523 --> 20:38.770
Do you know this mountain?

20:38.896 --> 20:40.819
It's my first time here.

20:41.445 --> 20:44.406
For someone who has traveled
to every corner of the country,

20:44.450 --> 20:46.783
are there still places
you're not familiar with?

20:46.852 --> 20:50.086
Because I only look
for the auspicious ones.

21:52.241 --> 21:54.351
The dragon's energy
stretches out far and wide!

21:54.351 --> 21:55.560
Good.

21:55.560 --> 21:58.379
Even North Korea is
visible from here. See?

21:58.380 --> 22:00.746
You can see North Korea.

22:03.746 --> 22:06.413
The grave looks plain
compared to its surroundings.

22:38.687 --> 22:40.480
Is there anything written there?

22:42.441 --> 22:43.900
It's unnamed.

22:55.162 --> 22:59.625
Could you please tell me
who suggested this burial site?

23:00.137 --> 23:02.002
A famous monk at the time.

23:02.002 --> 23:04.546
In recognition of my grandfather's
great contributions to the country,

23:05.547 --> 23:08.008
he told my father that he found the
most auspicious burial site for him.

23:08.008 --> 23:09.593
A monk?

23:09.593 --> 23:10.510
Yes.

23:10.510 --> 23:13.055
His Buddhist name was Gisune.

23:13.305 --> 23:14.806
Gisune?

23:15.144 --> 23:17.184
A very bizarre Buddhist name.

23:17.684 --> 23:20.812
But the grave looks quite plain.

23:21.313 --> 23:23.482
Grave robbers were rampant in those days,

23:23.482 --> 23:27.026
so I heard he was sent off
quietly in an unassuming manner.

23:36.328 --> 23:37.788
What do you think?

23:38.205 --> 23:40.040
Shall we set the date right away?

23:42.793 --> 23:45.212
What's wrong?

23:50.384 --> 23:51.802
Sir...

23:52.261 --> 23:55.722
I'm afraid I can't carry out this task.

23:58.558 --> 24:00.894
Here we go again.

24:00.894 --> 24:02.062
Sang-deok!

24:03.021 --> 24:04.940
- Who's he to decide?
- What's going on?

24:05.440 --> 24:07.067
Is it that bad?

24:07.734 --> 24:10.453
Isn't there some way to figure this out?

24:11.655 --> 24:13.532
Why aren't you saying anything?

24:15.867 --> 24:17.619
But...

24:17.619 --> 24:20.622
The mountain's shape is fine,
so what's the problem?

24:21.248 --> 24:24.209
Have you forgotten how much
this deal is worth?

24:25.309 --> 24:28.088
Sir, why are you doing this?

24:30.632 --> 24:32.759
You guys know all too well...

24:32.760 --> 24:35.720
...what happens when you disturb
a grave that shouldn't be meddled with.

24:35.721 --> 24:38.265
I've been digging up lands
for a living for 40 years,

24:38.265 --> 24:40.684
but this grave is like nothing
I've ever seen before.

24:40.684 --> 24:43.019
It's the most ominous place imaginable.

24:43.020 --> 24:47.399
A person should never be buried in a
place like this under any circumstances.

24:47.399 --> 24:50.152
If we mess with the wrong thing
in a place like that,

24:50.152 --> 24:54.322
everyone from the geomancer down to
the laborers will die one by one!

24:54.323 --> 24:55.880
Don't chime in unless you know
what you're talking about.

24:55.881 --> 24:58.076
Hwarim, you've seen the foxes, too.

25:00.203 --> 25:04.166
Foxes and graves don't mix,
it makes no sense.

25:05.939 --> 25:08.778
It's the most ominous place of them all.

25:18.388 --> 25:21.975
That was the last time I saw my son smiling.

25:22.844 --> 25:23.894
The truth is...

25:23.894 --> 25:25.812
I had two children before him,

25:25.812 --> 25:27.981
but both ended in miscarriages
for unknown reasons,

25:27.981 --> 25:30.192
so he was conceived late in life
after much effort.

25:31.944 --> 25:34.446
Professor Kim, do you have any children?

25:34.538 --> 25:36.615
Yes, I do.

25:36.615 --> 25:39.409
I have a daughter who's getting married soon.

25:39.910 --> 25:41.245
Congratulations.

25:41.536 --> 25:43.247
No need for that...

25:43.305 --> 25:45.666
Is your daughter in a similar line of work?

25:45.958 --> 25:48.585
My daughter majored in aerospace engineering at KAIST,

25:48.585 --> 25:51.421
and now she works for an airline in Germany.

25:51.713 --> 25:54.716
But now that she's getting married,
it's all chaos.

25:55.316 --> 25:56.218
Interesting.

25:57.052 --> 26:00.597
The father is a geomancer, while
the daughter is an aerospace engineer...

26:00.597 --> 26:01.890
Here's the thing.

26:01.890 --> 26:05.227
If you carefully analyze these two fields,

26:05.227 --> 26:08.814
you'll find many similar aspects.

26:08.814 --> 26:10.314
The concept of the Five Elements,

26:10.315 --> 26:15.027
it takes the earth as the starting point
and includes water, fire, metal and wood,

26:15.028 --> 26:18.073
which are studied as the essential
elements constituting nature.

26:18.073 --> 26:20.784
- And when it comes to aerospace engineering...
- Then...

26:22.953 --> 26:25.038
Please, save my son.

26:30.210 --> 26:33.337
Mr. Park Ji-yong, are you
keeping something from us?

26:35.799 --> 26:38.844
- What do you mean?
- 38.3417°,

26:38.917 --> 26:41.096
128.3189°.

26:41.096 --> 26:42.723
Latitude and longitude.

26:42.973 --> 26:45.392
The numbers engraved on the back of the gravestone.

26:45.684 --> 26:47.936
That monk named Gisune...

26:48.348 --> 26:50.772
I don't know who that fellow is,

26:50.842 --> 26:52.623
but he was unnervingly accurate.

26:52.624 --> 26:55.318
Evidently he had a clear purpose.

27:00.907 --> 27:02.326
No...

27:02.993 --> 27:04.077
I don't know.

27:05.370 --> 27:07.164
And I'm not hiding anything from any of you.

27:07.164 --> 27:09.625
I'll say this again.

27:09.625 --> 27:14.504
Relocating the grave from such a peculiar
and ominous place is extremely dangerous.

27:14.569 --> 27:16.781
It's like digging up a landmine
with your bare hands.

27:16.782 --> 27:19.799
Let's substitute the negative
energy through a ritual.

27:21.595 --> 27:23.472
I knew it.

27:25.641 --> 27:28.518
We'll perform the ritual and
relocate the grave simultaneously.

27:29.061 --> 27:31.605
Why are you acting like this?
You already knew the answer.

27:32.022 --> 27:34.566
I don't believe in things I haven't tried.

27:34.633 --> 27:37.168
Although it would be the first time doing
the ritual while relocating the grave,

27:37.169 --> 27:39.854
in theory, it's not impossible.

27:40.101 --> 27:41.156
Wait a minute.

27:42.366 --> 27:46.453
Why are we asking Professor Kim
for permission?

27:46.620 --> 27:48.980
It's not like he's the only geomancer in Korea.

27:49.206 --> 27:51.641
That's why it's hard to work with old geezers.

27:51.642 --> 27:52.042
Hey...

27:52.042 --> 27:55.078
Look, he says his child is sick. Okay?

28:03.262 --> 28:05.597
This hotel has good positioning.

28:07.516 --> 28:08.809
- Good.
- Let's go!

28:08.809 --> 28:12.688
 It's a sort of deceitful ritual,
also called "redirecting the misfortune". 

28:13.063 --> 28:17.442
 First, we create a connection between 5 workers
born in the year of the Pig and 5 pigs, 

28:18.110 --> 28:20.654
 then we let the 5 men dig up the grave. 

28:21.238 --> 28:24.241
 The principle is to direct the negative energy
emerging from the earth towards the 5 animals, 

28:24.241 --> 28:26.535
 which I will then dissipate. 

28:28.521 --> 28:30.471
Your aunt is here.

28:30.471 --> 28:35.121
It seems like your mother shared what's happening.

29:11.941 --> 29:16.061
 In the year of the Water Tiger, 

29:16.501 --> 29:20.981
 on the new moon of October, 

29:21.431 --> 29:25.221
 I, Go Young-geun, 

29:25.301 --> 29:28.940
 respectfully stand in the presence of 

29:28.941 --> 29:33.251
 the deceased Mr. Park from Miryang. 

29:33.431 --> 29:37.411
 May the spirits grant protection. 

29:37.741 --> 29:41.701
 Let there be no future hardships. 

29:42.121 --> 29:44.561
 Please accept these offerings. 

29:50.161 --> 29:55.391
 33 realms of the heavenly palace,
28 constellations of the earthly palace 

29:55.431 --> 30:01.041
 In the 33 realms where all Buddhas and
heavenly beings dwell, everything aligns 

30:03.411 --> 30:09.011
 Our great ancestor ascended to the throne
after the founding of the Joseon dynasty 

30:09.021 --> 30:14.661
 Our foundation faces southward,
in alignment with the solar noon 

30:14.701 --> 30:19.981
 Mount Gwanak is our guide,
Mount Inwang becomes the Azure Dragon 

30:19.981 --> 30:23.871
 Stretching ten thousand li to the east,
behold the White Tiger! 

30:30.831 --> 30:32.371
Let's go!

30:39.141 --> 30:42.531
Let's go!

30:44.721 --> 30:46.901
Let's go!

30:57.141 --> 30:59.381
Let's go!

31:19.651 --> 31:21.621
Very good!

31:28.061 --> 31:31.591
- Up the mountain!
- Up the mountain!

31:38.041 --> 31:39.541
Exhumation!

31:40.241 --> 31:41.781
Exhumation!

31:42.151 --> 31:44.081
Exhumation!

33:31.401 --> 33:33.091
There it is.

33:41.491 --> 33:43.001
The grave has been opened!

33:43.151 --> 33:45.001
The grave has been opened!

33:50.484 --> 33:52.069
Thank you for your hard work.

33:52.069 --> 33:54.321
My goodness.

33:58.319 --> 34:00.535
The cold here is brutal.

34:16.468 --> 34:19.221
It's been so long, it's barely visible.

34:34.486 --> 34:37.239
Wait, what is this?

34:37.395 --> 34:39.783
Hey, it's a juniper wood coffin!

34:39.783 --> 34:42.411
In the past, only the royal
family used this kind of wood.

34:42.411 --> 34:43.899
We had something like this here?

34:43.900 --> 34:44.663
For real?

34:46.957 --> 34:48.875
Lifting the coffin!

34:51.920 --> 34:53.422
Yes, that's good.

34:53.422 --> 34:55.306
Just like that. With a little more strength!

34:55.307 --> 34:56.133
Lower it.

34:56.133 --> 34:58.406
- Slowly, slowly.
- Lower.

34:58.480 --> 35:00.846
The coffin must be loaded intact
into the hearse.

35:00.846 --> 35:02.592
We're going straight to the crematorium.

35:02.665 --> 35:05.851
You fellas bury the gravestone
and wrap up everything here.

35:06.187 --> 35:08.228
Let's change the ropes.

35:08.341 --> 35:09.728
And don't eat meat today.

35:09.828 --> 35:11.898
Yes.

35:16.862 --> 35:20.139
I'm leaving after handling it
with consideration.

35:28.081 --> 35:29.166
Yes.

35:29.791 --> 35:32.752
A deceased person lies inside
and we can't even shroud his corpse.

35:32.753 --> 35:33.962
Let's at least show him the proper respect.

35:34.379 --> 35:36.381
Gosh...

35:36.673 --> 35:39.801
I'm the man who even shrouded
the corpse of an ex-president.

35:40.135 --> 35:42.933
It's all over now. Loosen up, okay?

35:58.194 --> 35:59.321
Let's see...

36:00.948 --> 36:02.282
There's nothing there.

36:02.282 --> 36:03.575
Let's go.

36:13.293 --> 36:14.561
What's this?

36:14.699 --> 36:15.254
Shit!

37:03.218 --> 37:05.012
What is this?

37:05.304 --> 37:07.639
Unbelievable.

37:19.401 --> 37:22.112
- I'll talk to him.
- Then I'll call the director.

37:26.158 --> 37:27.159
Mr. Park.

37:27.159 --> 37:29.479
It suddenly started
raining out of the blue,

37:29.586 --> 37:31.872
so we'll have to delay
the cremation for a while.

37:33.081 --> 37:34.416
How come?

37:34.594 --> 37:36.441
It's not like we're cremating him outdoors.

37:36.442 --> 37:40.088
If cremated on a rainy day,

37:40.380 --> 37:43.091
the deceased won't be able
to depart to a good place.

37:43.383 --> 37:46.261
Call it superstition if you want,

37:46.261 --> 37:49.155
but I'm telling you this as a
matter of professional ethics.

37:50.769 --> 37:53.352
These things do happen sometimes, yes.

37:53.519 --> 37:54.811
In such cases,

37:54.949 --> 37:58.023
the remains are placed at
the morgue of a nearby hospital,

37:58.108 --> 38:00.984
and the cremation is scheduled
for the next auspicious day.

38:01.360 --> 38:04.947
If we go to the hospital, won't
we have to file a funeral report?

38:05.005 --> 38:06.239
Sang-deok!

38:06.319 --> 38:08.499
Sang-deok, I just got off the phone,
it's all taken care of!

38:08.500 --> 38:09.819
You can go straight away!

38:09.939 --> 38:11.453
Don't worry about that.

38:11.825 --> 38:13.763
We're acquainted with the staff there.

38:17.368 --> 38:20.003
What do you mean by bringing an
unopened coffin after relocating the grave?

38:20.099 --> 38:22.714
Apparently the chief mourner
doesn't allow us to open it.

38:22.799 --> 38:26.218
- Here you go.
- Oh, no need.

38:26.353 --> 38:27.719
What in the world?

38:27.887 --> 38:28.791
What's wrong with you?

38:28.792 --> 38:32.266
- Take it, quickly.
- Gosh...

38:32.599 --> 38:35.602
The last team just left today, so it's quiet.

38:35.700 --> 38:37.312
Oh, that's good.

38:37.390 --> 38:40.065
My goodness... Rain on the cremation day...

38:40.181 --> 38:43.110
It's difficult for him to depart
for the other world.

38:51.456 --> 38:54.496
- Do we need to set a new date?
- Yes.

38:55.747 --> 38:58.458
But can you really trust those people?

38:58.667 --> 39:01.961
I gave them just enough and
told them only what was necessary.

39:01.962 --> 39:03.955
There is no need for concern.

39:04.423 --> 39:06.883
Now that we have some time,

39:07.467 --> 39:11.513
let's think of a way to bury him
peacefully at the Yeoju Cemetery.

39:12.431 --> 39:15.475
I'm still against the idea of cremating him.

39:16.184 --> 39:19.146
He's my father, so I have the right to decide.

39:20.856 --> 39:22.316
Go get some rest for now.

39:27.964 --> 39:30.257
Since you're not allowed to open the coffin,

39:30.376 --> 39:32.134
you can just leave it here.

39:32.176 --> 39:34.953
I just need to set the humidity.

39:35.033 --> 39:36.243
Thank you.

39:36.835 --> 39:38.879
Wow... This coffin...

39:39.875 --> 39:43.044
The deceased must have held
a high position in the government.

39:43.170 --> 39:44.588
- How have you been?
- Hey, it's been a while.

39:47.069 --> 39:49.676
The chief mourner and the rest of
the family have all gone back to Seoul.

39:50.558 --> 39:53.472
Hwarim says she's on her way here.

39:54.226 --> 39:56.058
Since it's freezing outside,

39:56.058 --> 39:58.477
you should go and have
a bowl of hot soup.

39:59.603 --> 40:01.688
I'll be back after going somewhere.

40:02.022 --> 40:03.065
All right.

40:22.802 --> 40:26.102
BOGUKSA TEMPLE

40:57.552 --> 41:00.742
I don't think we've met before.
How may I help you?

41:00.743 --> 41:02.291
Oh, excuse me.

41:02.791 --> 41:06.920
I was passing by and saw
the sign on the road.

41:07.064 --> 41:09.339
Oh, I see.

41:09.449 --> 41:10.585
I'm here because...

41:10.586 --> 41:13.755
The sign for Boguksa Temple is
marked with a feng shui symbol.

41:13.756 --> 41:16.221
It seemed a bit strange,
so I thought I'd stop by.

41:18.164 --> 41:19.391
Are you a geomancer?

41:19.391 --> 41:20.767
Yes.

41:20.885 --> 41:23.937
I was a disciple of Master Choi Eui-jung.

41:24.438 --> 41:28.466
Even though currently I'm barely making
a living on my own by digging the earth.

41:28.467 --> 41:30.578
It may look worn out now,

41:30.651 --> 41:33.405
but this place has been around
for over 100 years.

41:33.739 --> 41:37.242
The head monk who first
built this temple here

41:37.242 --> 41:41.204
was very skilled in feng shui
and made quite a name for himself.

41:41.326 --> 41:42.956
Oh, I see.

41:43.037 --> 41:46.126
I can tell just by looking at this place.

41:46.126 --> 41:47.502
So, I was wondering...

41:47.753 --> 41:50.664
The name of that head monk...

41:50.756 --> 41:53.082
Is it Gisune, by any chance?

41:53.425 --> 41:54.718
Gisune?

41:55.010 --> 41:57.179
No, he was Venerable Wonbong.

41:57.679 --> 42:00.182
But why do you ask?

42:00.182 --> 42:01.350
Ah...

42:01.683 --> 42:05.103
On top of that mountain over there,

42:05.395 --> 42:07.648
there is an unnamed grave.

42:07.744 --> 42:10.651
- Do you happen to know anything about...
- Of course.

42:11.068 --> 42:13.653
I'm not sure if it's still talked about,

42:13.654 --> 42:17.313
but I heard numerous rumors
a long time ago.

42:19.201 --> 42:21.453
What kind of rumors?

42:21.525 --> 42:23.372
Instead of sitting alone in the dark,

42:23.372 --> 42:25.999
why don't you go across the street
and have a bowl of beef soup?

42:26.097 --> 42:27.417
Sure, don't worry.

42:27.493 --> 42:29.604
- Okay, I'm leaving.
- Good job. See you.

42:33.251 --> 42:36.218
Why do they always insist
on deciding the menu for me?

42:43.809 --> 42:47.896
 There was a rumor of a treasure
buried inside that grave. 

42:48.563 --> 42:50.023
 A treasure? 

42:51.882 --> 42:55.355
Another rumor claimed that the grave belonged
to the wealthiest man from the Joseon era.

42:55.356 --> 42:58.322
There were also rumors suggesting
it was an unknown royal tomb.

42:58.323 --> 43:02.411
That's why, in the past, many grave
robbers were lurking around it.

43:03.537 --> 43:04.788
Grave robbers?

43:04.962 --> 43:07.374
But they were all suddenly captured, and...

43:07.470 --> 43:10.754
Apparently a few of them crossed the
border to the North, or something.

43:10.755 --> 43:12.987
So in the end, they failed to rob it?

43:13.080 --> 43:15.103
They likely didn't even get
a chance to attempt it.

43:15.104 --> 43:17.718
Perhaps due to being a high-ranking
person's grave, it was heavily guarded.

43:17.718 --> 43:19.545
I heard they couldn't even get close to it.

43:21.179 --> 43:22.180
These are...

43:22.180 --> 43:25.350
The tools those people left behind.

43:32.525 --> 43:33.525
But...

43:33.942 --> 43:35.944
Why are you asking about that grave?

43:40.490 --> 43:42.408
Today, I...

43:42.409 --> 43:45.011
...dug up that grave.

43:51.627 --> 43:52.836
And well?

43:53.420 --> 43:55.339
Was there a treasure buried there?

44:11.546 --> 44:12.272
Excuse me!

44:12.326 --> 44:13.899
What are you doing?

44:14.799 --> 44:15.275
Hey!

44:20.656 --> 44:22.449
Professor...

44:22.449 --> 44:23.533
Professor!

44:23.909 --> 44:24.785
Hey!

44:25.502 --> 44:30.502
CHAPTER III: SPIRIT

44:31.708 --> 44:32.834
What?

44:32.834 --> 44:33.961
What do you mean?

44:33.961 --> 44:35.420
The coffin has been opened?

44:36.771 --> 44:38.768
He and his damned hands...

44:38.848 --> 44:40.832
I've given him plenty, he really
shouldn't be doing things like that.

44:40.833 --> 44:42.852
No wonder he's got such an off-putting stare.

44:44.930 --> 44:45.847
Oh...

44:45.847 --> 44:47.266
What happened?

44:48.600 --> 44:50.660
Something passed by her side.

44:51.728 --> 44:53.138
What exactly passed by?

45:02.948 --> 45:05.117
Something came out of there.

45:05.712 --> 45:07.160
Something very threatening.

45:46.273 --> 45:48.952
Dad...

45:50.621 --> 45:54.833
My dad...

45:58.837 --> 46:00.714
Jong-soon...

46:01.798 --> 46:03.967
My son...

46:05.594 --> 46:08.263
Open up for me, please.

46:09.222 --> 46:12.100
Dad...

46:14.004 --> 46:17.439
Come in.

46:45.807 --> 46:47.594
Dad...

47:23.736 --> 47:29.344
Our smart little puppy...

47:31.110 --> 47:35.767
Here it flows with milk and honey,

47:37.227 --> 47:43.275
while your father is hungry and cold.

47:43.327 --> 47:46.028
Forgive me...

48:49.424 --> 48:52.427
 The spirit is probably wandering
wildly at this very moment. 

48:52.427 --> 48:54.346
 The chief mourner will be in danger. 

48:54.346 --> 48:57.724
Professor, please go to Seoul
quickly ahead of me.

48:57.823 --> 49:00.894
Meanwhile, we will summon
the spirit back here.

49:00.894 --> 49:03.621
Hold on, are you going to
summon it back here?

49:03.734 --> 49:06.149
For a century it wailed
from beneath the ground,

49:06.149 --> 49:08.193
yet no one pulled it out.

49:08.652 --> 49:11.279
The spirit harbors nothing but hatred.

49:11.280 --> 49:14.533
It will hunt down all of its relatives.

49:22.012 --> 49:23.959
Talk about a mood killer...

49:24.066 --> 49:26.545
Outside it's raining, the coffin lid
gets opened, a ghost comes out...

49:26.692 --> 49:28.380
I really don't wanna do this...

49:28.467 --> 49:31.008
What on earth is going on?

49:33.719 --> 49:37.179
Is it all right to do this on the same
day as the energy redirecting ritual?

49:37.180 --> 49:38.932
It's fine.

49:40.017 --> 49:42.185
Elder Go, you must get the timing right.

49:42.394 --> 49:44.896
- You need to take hold of it as soon as it enters.
- Got it.

49:58.631 --> 50:01.931
 In the Sahā world of endurance,
the land of all living things. 

50:01.932 --> 50:05.631
 The Joseon Dynasty of the
East Sea, the Republic of Korea. 

50:05.671 --> 50:08.671
 Gangwon Province, 26 Bureaus; 

50:08.672 --> 50:12.081
 The county is Goseong, 

50:12.131 --> 50:15.831
 and the township is Jukwang. 

50:15.861 --> 50:21.731
 We've come to officiate the rites
for the deceased of the Park family. 

50:21.781 --> 50:23.081
 At the first altar,
five spirits; 

50:23.082 --> 50:24.381
 At the second altar,
one thousand catties; 

50:24.382 --> 50:28.161
 At the third altar is the soul-summoning
space, please return quickly. 

50:28.162 --> 50:31.391
 Return to the space between
the physical and spiritual world, 

50:31.392 --> 50:34.991
 return to the space between life and death. 

50:37.681 --> 50:38.921
Come, come quickly!

50:41.731 --> 50:47.561
 Is it perhaps difficult to return
due to the water being too deep? 

50:47.601 --> 50:53.361
 Or is it due to an illness that you
are bedridden and unable to return? 

50:53.401 --> 50:54.111
 You should... 

51:02.474 --> 51:05.936
 If you can't return because you have
no clothes, return wearing mourning clothes. 

51:05.936 --> 51:08.647
 If you can't return because you have
no crutches, return using a bamboo cane. 

51:08.647 --> 51:12.567
 If you can't return because you have
no shoes, return wearing straw shoes. 

51:12.567 --> 51:16.780
 If you can't return because you're thirsty,
return after drinking 3 glasses of alcohol. 

51:16.780 --> 51:19.533
 If you can't return because you have no dwelling,
you are welcome at the shaman's residence. 

51:19.533 --> 51:21.733
 If you can't return because
your body has decayed, 

51:21.734 --> 51:23.704
 let your spirit grab onto
the pine needle branch. 

51:23.704 --> 51:25.664
 If you can't return
because you can't speak, 

51:25.664 --> 51:28.408
 borrow the shaman's voice
and return, even if only for a moment. 

51:28.409 --> 51:30.877
 Reflecting on the past and present, 

51:30.877 --> 51:34.590
 we all get gray hair and the
only inevitable thing is death. 

51:35.090 --> 51:36.883
Possess him!

51:36.883 --> 51:39.845
Yes, it's coming, it's on its way!

51:43.734 --> 51:47.520
- It possessed him, he's possessed!
- Bong-gil!

51:47.614 --> 51:49.100
Let it in!

52:24.813 --> 52:25.933
Grandpa...

52:27.225 --> 52:28.727
Who are you?

52:29.853 --> 52:30.854
Well?

52:32.314 --> 52:33.748
Bong-gil, don't let it escape!

52:36.510 --> 52:37.819
Oh, dear...

52:38.303 --> 52:40.322
What made you feel so wronged?

52:40.761 --> 52:42.032
Let's hear it.

52:42.394 --> 52:43.689
- Well?
- Shit...

52:43.742 --> 52:46.869
Vent out all your repressed anger
here today before you leave.

52:46.870 --> 52:49.456
Don't go anywhere else.

52:50.582 --> 52:52.626
My kin...

52:53.335 --> 52:55.087
I'm taking them with me.

52:58.301 --> 53:00.676
You can't do that.

53:27.710 --> 53:28.737
We've lost it.

53:29.454 --> 53:30.747
What do we do now?

53:38.490 --> 53:39.506
Hello?

53:40.038 --> 53:41.688
Ah, it's me, Kim Sang-deok, sir.

53:41.768 --> 53:43.135
Is everything all right?

53:43.969 --> 53:44.970
Yes.

53:45.220 --> 53:46.680
How may I help you?

53:46.827 --> 53:48.390
Oh, I'm glad.

53:48.390 --> 53:50.809
Well, something came up, and...

53:50.901 --> 53:52.969
I'm rushing over to you right now.

53:53.452 --> 53:55.562
I know it's late, but can
we talk for a moment?

53:55.622 --> 53:56.481
Sure.

53:57.357 --> 53:58.859
What's going on?

53:59.811 --> 54:02.946
Mr. Park Ji-yong, you are staying
at the same hotel as before, right?

54:03.063 --> 54:04.590
Yes, I'm almost there.

54:04.676 --> 54:06.622
I'll head up shortly.

54:06.702 --> 54:07.784
Hold on.

54:08.336 --> 54:09.411
Who is it?

54:09.563 --> 54:11.114
Yes, it's me, Kim Sang-deok!

54:11.681 --> 54:12.708
What?

54:12.788 --> 54:13.999
Hello?

54:14.069 --> 54:16.001
What is it? What happened?

54:16.420 --> 54:18.091
Professor Kim, are you already at the door?

54:18.151 --> 54:20.005
Excuse me! Director Park!

54:20.235 --> 54:22.419
Ah, no, no, no! No!

54:22.539 --> 54:23.807
That's not me.

54:23.907 --> 54:26.099
This is happening because your
grandfather's coffin has been opened.

54:26.100 --> 54:27.151
Mr. Park Ji-yong!

54:27.237 --> 54:28.914
It's an urgent matter,
please open the door!

54:29.001 --> 54:31.043
- My grandfather's coffin?
- Ah, yes...

54:31.116 --> 54:33.090
I apologize for the way
things have developed.

54:33.091 --> 54:34.757
Has anything happened inside?

54:34.758 --> 54:35.945
With that said,

54:35.946 --> 54:38.274
do not open that door under any
circumstances and stay still.

54:38.275 --> 54:39.900
- I'm almost there.
- Mr. Park Ji-yong!

54:39.900 --> 54:41.517
From this moment on,

54:41.518 --> 54:44.078
you must follow only my
instructions and remain calm.

54:44.805 --> 54:46.490
Mr. Park Ji-yong, listen carefully.

54:46.580 --> 54:49.868
Move away from the door and
take shelter near the window.

54:52.079 --> 54:53.420
Open the door, first.

54:54.158 --> 54:56.579
It's urgent, I need to explain the
situation to you as soon as possible!

54:56.580 --> 54:57.857
Don't answer him.

54:57.858 --> 54:59.370
Don't even listen to him!

54:59.371 --> 55:01.817
First, go to the window and open it.

55:01.883 --> 55:03.579
Your grandfather will protect you,

55:03.652 --> 55:05.006
you just have to let him in.

55:05.007 --> 55:06.773
Excuse me! Mr. Park!

55:06.880 --> 55:08.720
Trust me! Hurry up!

55:12.606 --> 55:14.977
Open it!

55:54.992 --> 55:56.101
Mr. Park Ji-yong!

56:01.513 --> 56:02.608
Mr. Park Ji-yong.

56:08.572 --> 56:09.448
Are you all right?

56:16.553 --> 56:19.249
Admirable young people of the peninsula!

56:20.000 --> 56:23.962
Do you hear the roar of
hundreds of planes and cannons?

56:24.630 --> 56:27.049
March forth, sons of the Empire!

56:28.335 --> 56:32.787
Lift your silver guns and swords in
the radiant glow of the Rising Sun Flag!

56:33.263 --> 56:35.915
For the new unity
of Greater East Asia,

56:36.224 --> 56:40.695
offer your very beings
to the great Empire!

56:52.407 --> 56:53.450
Ambulance...

56:53.784 --> 56:55.410
Call an ambulance...

56:55.911 --> 56:57.788
Please call an ambulance.

56:57.844 --> 56:58.830
Okay?

56:59.206 --> 57:00.832
Call an ambulance!

57:06.755 --> 57:09.169
I saw it with my own eyes!

57:09.242 --> 57:11.448
If we just stand by, it'll be
one funeral after another.

57:11.449 --> 57:13.512
- I'm going to the crematorium!
- Okay, go!

57:13.572 --> 57:17.015
And you need to get the cremation
consent, I'll be right there on standby.

57:36.910 --> 57:38.287
Right now...

57:38.829 --> 57:42.415
- Your grandfather's coffin has been...
- The fox has broken the tiger's spine.

57:43.317 --> 57:44.501
Excuse me?

57:51.057 --> 57:53.617
The fox has broken the tiger's spine.

58:07.449 --> 58:10.068
I said the fox has broken the tiger's spine.

58:37.577 --> 58:38.513
Mother-in-law.

58:38.603 --> 58:40.807
Are you not feeling well?

58:41.892 --> 58:44.519
She must be worn out from
her trip to the countryside.

58:45.771 --> 58:47.814
I need to rest for a bit.

58:53.912 --> 58:57.262
Joseph's condition seems to be
better today, doesn't it?

58:57.312 --> 59:01.232
Eunice, I cannot reach anyone at home,
so I'll go back home and check.

59:01.402 --> 59:03.432
Sure, I'll be here.

59:09.211 --> 59:11.193
Buddy, I'm asking you this
because it's urgent!

59:11.194 --> 59:12.521
When have I ever asked you
for such a favor?

59:12.522 --> 59:13.936
Bro, now is really not the time!

59:13.937 --> 59:16.436
I'll be there shortly,
so please hurry, will you?

59:16.437 --> 59:18.916
And with this rain pouring down,
what's this about a cremation?

59:18.917 --> 59:19.855
What does the chief mourner
have to say about this?

59:19.856 --> 59:22.057
Something's come out of the coffin, man!

59:22.122 --> 59:23.934
You get what I'm saying, right?

59:24.393 --> 59:26.061
It needs to be cremated immediately.

59:26.715 --> 59:28.647
Please contact the family
in the US right away.

59:28.648 --> 59:29.648
Excuse me?

59:30.038 --> 59:30.971
What do you mean?

59:31.057 --> 59:32.435
You saw it too.

59:32.515 --> 59:34.911
The baby is the next one in danger.

59:35.195 --> 59:38.003
 On the treetop, 

59:38.116 --> 59:40.487
 when the wind blows, 

59:40.547 --> 59:43.161
 the cradle will rock. 

59:43.537 --> 59:45.956
 When the bough breaks, 

59:45.956 --> 59:49.376
 the cradle will fall, 

59:49.626 --> 59:53.434
 and down will come baby, 

59:53.520 --> 59:56.717
 cradle, and all. 

01:00:01.861 --> 01:00:04.474
No one is answering the phone
at the US residence.

01:00:05.976 --> 01:00:07.477
Then...

01:00:27.205 --> 01:00:28.292
What is this?

01:00:28.293 --> 01:00:30.500
You didn't shroud the corpse
after relocating the grave?

01:00:30.792 --> 01:00:32.461
Are you planning to burn it entirely?

01:00:33.545 --> 01:00:36.632
If the district office finds out
about this, there will be an uproar.

01:00:41.781 --> 01:00:43.011
My father's coffin?

01:00:43.091 --> 01:00:45.250
Yes, I don't know the reason either.

01:00:45.343 --> 01:00:47.559
But they said it has to
be cremated immediately.

01:00:47.976 --> 01:00:49.227
What does that mean?

01:00:50.133 --> 01:00:51.353
Hello, ma'am.

01:00:51.354 --> 01:00:52.980
We need to act fast.

01:00:52.981 --> 01:00:57.027
Your father is heading towards
the newborn in the US as we speak.

01:01:18.845 --> 01:01:20.460
- I'll cremate him.
- No, wait.

01:01:20.533 --> 01:01:22.701
The representative of the bereaved family
hasn't given consent yet, wait a moment.

01:01:22.702 --> 01:01:24.873
There's no one answering the
phone at the US residence.

01:01:24.874 --> 01:01:28.392
Therefore, you need to give us
permission to cremate him.

01:01:48.912 --> 01:01:51.748
Is this really the only way?

01:02:09.679 --> 01:02:10.762
All right.

01:02:11.435 --> 01:02:12.853
Cremate him.

01:02:12.932 --> 01:02:14.062
Yes.

01:02:16.280 --> 01:02:17.399
Burn it.

01:02:40.592 --> 01:02:42.798
Oh dear, what a tragic fate...

01:02:42.799 --> 01:02:45.043
He won't be able to depart to a good place.

01:03:32.777 --> 01:03:38.689
 Hitting the road 

01:03:39.329 --> 01:03:45.195
 Hitting the road 

01:03:46.697 --> 01:03:52.911
 The beach roses along
Myeongsasimni's shores 

01:03:52.911 --> 01:03:58.500
 They wither, their leaves fall,
harbor no sorrow 

01:03:58.630 --> 01:04:04.590
 Oh-oh, oh-oh 

01:04:04.667 --> 01:04:10.637
 Oh-oh, oh-oh, hey, oh-ho 

01:04:10.704 --> 01:04:15.475
 Which enlightened being
started it all? 

01:04:15.565 --> 01:04:20.522
 Why did the notion of death
come into existence? 

01:04:20.607 --> 01:04:26.028
 Oh-ho, oh-ho 

01:04:26.328 --> 01:04:31.028
 Oh-oh, oh-oh, hey, oh-ho 

01:04:32.674 --> 01:04:35.746
 You've deviated from the route,
restarting the search. 

01:04:38.952 --> 01:04:41.152
CHAPTER IV: SPIRITUAL RETRIBUTION
(DISTURBED EARTH)

01:04:41.153 --> 01:04:42.711
Sang-deok, you know Chang-min, right?

01:04:43.045 --> 01:04:44.809
After relocating that grave,

01:04:44.896 --> 01:04:46.965
he seems to have gotten quite sick.

01:04:47.115 --> 01:04:49.885
Stop by and see him
when you have time, okay?

01:04:49.931 --> 01:04:52.596
 Turn left 

01:04:52.737 --> 01:04:54.868
The hospital can't figure
out what's wrong, either.

01:04:54.869 --> 01:04:57.225
They just keep doing tests
and draining my wallet.

01:04:58.226 --> 01:04:59.886
I have these sinister dreams...

01:05:01.254 --> 01:05:02.648
I even see things...

01:05:03.982 --> 01:05:05.025
Sang-deok...

01:05:07.856 --> 01:05:11.954
I think it's retribution
for having angered a spirit.

01:05:11.955 --> 01:05:13.431
It's just that...

01:05:13.511 --> 01:05:16.245
Right after the exhumation
that day, I saw something.

01:05:16.703 --> 01:05:18.914
It looked strange.

01:05:19.373 --> 01:05:20.123
That snake...

01:05:21.375 --> 01:05:23.109
What? A snake?

01:05:23.110 --> 01:05:26.338
Damn it, I should have just ignored it.

01:05:27.381 --> 01:05:28.507
Sang-deok.

01:05:28.618 --> 01:05:30.267
I want to ask you a favor.

01:05:30.739 --> 01:05:34.638
Please find that snake cut in half,
and perform a ritual offering for it.

01:05:38.841 --> 01:05:41.186
 I really didn't want
to go there that day. 

01:05:41.402 --> 01:05:42.813
 I truly didn't. 

01:05:43.313 --> 01:05:44.356
Sang-deok.

01:05:44.648 --> 01:05:47.795
Something there felt off from the
very beginning, don't you think so?

01:05:47.796 --> 01:05:49.861
Why would there be a grave
in such a place?

01:07:35.259 --> 01:07:36.677
Stacked coffins.

01:07:37.302 --> 01:07:39.471
Yes... I'm busy now.

01:07:39.569 --> 01:07:41.265
I'm studying the Bible with
some people from the church.

01:07:41.332 --> 01:07:42.271
50,000 won.

01:07:42.345 --> 01:07:43.600
Here you go.

01:07:43.699 --> 01:07:44.643
Deal.

01:07:44.851 --> 01:07:45.852
What?

01:07:48.480 --> 01:07:49.467
Stacked coffins?!

01:07:49.523 --> 01:07:51.775
Yes, it was right underneath.

01:07:51.911 --> 01:07:53.568
But... Elder Go.

01:07:54.152 --> 01:07:56.947
Have you ever seen a coffin
standing vertically?

01:08:00.895 --> 01:08:01.910
Hello.

01:08:03.912 --> 01:08:05.330
Professor Hwarim?

01:08:06.081 --> 01:08:08.208
Now the V-ups.

01:08:08.209 --> 01:08:09.751
In a two-beat rhythm.

01:08:23.348 --> 01:08:27.494
When the ground shifts, it does
end up vertically sometimes, but...

01:08:29.278 --> 01:08:31.064
Isn't it too big?

01:08:32.190 --> 01:08:33.775
What's this?

01:08:39.281 --> 01:08:41.158
What's that thing?

01:08:49.965 --> 01:08:50.751
These...

01:08:52.336 --> 01:08:55.880
It seems these were placed to
prevent opening from the outside.

01:08:56.256 --> 01:08:58.133
- Or if not...
- If not, what?

01:08:58.508 --> 01:09:00.629
Probably the other way around.

01:09:03.329 --> 01:09:04.961
First, let's pull it out
and have a look.

01:09:04.962 --> 01:09:06.555
We're not pulling anything out.

01:09:06.556 --> 01:09:09.019
First, the right thing to do
is to inform the chief mourner.

01:09:09.019 --> 01:09:10.668
We have to talk about our money as well.

01:09:10.735 --> 01:09:11.813
Let's...

01:09:12.615 --> 01:09:15.107
Let's not meddle with this.

01:09:19.050 --> 01:09:20.662
Let's pull it out, first.

01:09:20.663 --> 01:09:22.850
He has to be a family member.

01:09:22.930 --> 01:09:25.661
We can't just leave this fellow here.

01:09:26.787 --> 01:09:28.997
But this thing, how...

01:09:29.116 --> 01:09:30.791
Let's just pull it out, go get the rope.

01:09:30.863 --> 01:09:32.793
The sun is setting.

01:09:36.093 --> 01:09:38.468
When I say one, two, three, pull hard.

01:09:38.608 --> 01:09:41.218
One! Two! Three!

01:09:56.108 --> 01:09:58.093
Is that even a human's coffin?

01:10:47.103 --> 01:10:48.744
Where are we going?

01:10:54.552 --> 01:10:55.952
BOGUKSA TEMPLE

01:11:08.430 --> 01:11:09.598
What is happening?

01:11:09.677 --> 01:11:13.727
As I've told you on the phone,
I had to relocate a grave unexpectedly.

01:11:13.903 --> 01:11:16.188
I will remain indebted to
you for your help today.

01:11:18.489 --> 01:11:21.192
The chief mourner said
she's on her way here.

01:11:21.193 --> 01:11:24.671
Is there a suitable area
where we could place the coffin?

01:11:43.741 --> 01:11:45.108
What on earth...

01:11:45.509 --> 01:11:47.761
This... what is this?

01:11:49.610 --> 01:11:54.434
Excuse me, Venerable, but do you
happen to have some glutinous rice?

01:12:10.649 --> 01:12:11.490
Bong-gil.

01:12:11.555 --> 01:12:13.453
Go to the car and bring the horse blood.

01:12:18.500 --> 01:12:21.294
You know this can't be anything good.

01:12:25.927 --> 01:12:27.822
What do you mean by stacked coffins?

01:12:27.823 --> 01:12:30.176
What in the world is that thing?

01:12:30.177 --> 01:12:34.141
Please tell us everything you know.

01:12:34.262 --> 01:12:35.601
I don't know.

01:12:36.059 --> 01:12:38.604
I really don't.

01:12:40.322 --> 01:12:42.816
I don't know why that thing
was buried there,

01:12:43.048 --> 01:12:48.100
and I don't know why my father's grave
was in such a terrible place, either.

01:12:48.384 --> 01:12:51.325
I saw what was inscribed
on the funeral banner.

01:12:52.166 --> 01:12:56.037
"Marquess Park Geun-hyun,
Vice Chairman of the Privy Council."

01:12:56.038 --> 01:13:01.083
Your father was infamous for
selling out our country.

01:13:01.248 --> 01:13:04.370
So as punishment, that monk
chose for your father the most...

01:13:04.436 --> 01:13:06.256
I know!

01:13:07.341 --> 01:13:09.259
That's why I don't know anything else.

01:13:11.430 --> 01:13:13.513
That monk named Gisune...

01:13:15.454 --> 01:13:17.476
He wasn't Korean.

01:13:18.894 --> 01:13:20.979
He was Japanese.

01:13:21.544 --> 01:13:23.389
- What?!
- He was Japanese?

01:13:23.440 --> 01:13:24.726
His name was...

01:13:24.727 --> 01:13:27.069
Murayama Junji.

01:13:29.071 --> 01:13:33.872
I heard he knew every corner of Joseon's
eight provinces like the back of his hand.

01:13:33.873 --> 01:13:39.102
So why would he choose such an ominous burial
site for my father who had been loyal to them?

01:13:39.103 --> 01:13:41.407
I just can't wrap my head around it.

01:13:45.128 --> 01:13:48.340
I've been notified that the baby
in the US is feeling well.

01:13:49.049 --> 01:13:52.511
I will prepare the remuneration
that Ji-yong promised to you.

01:13:52.844 --> 01:13:55.420
And as for that coffin...

01:13:55.421 --> 01:13:58.408
Take care of it as you see fit.

01:13:58.993 --> 01:14:01.311
 As I have learned, the Buddha
spoke of preserving life. 

01:14:01.375 --> 01:14:03.689
 To relieve the suffering and illness,
recite this scripture with reverence. 

01:14:03.689 --> 01:14:06.858
 Invoking the spirit of the Wood Dragon
to remove earthly misfortunes. 

01:14:06.957 --> 01:14:10.279
 Seven thousand Buddhas shall
deliver us from life's adversities. 

01:14:10.279 --> 01:14:12.948
 Invoking the spirit of the Wood Tiger
to liberate us from entanglements. 

01:14:13.017 --> 01:14:15.828
 Seven thousand Buddhas shall break us
free from mental and spiritual constraints, 

01:14:15.829 --> 01:14:19.245
 and through the sexagenary cycle
we shall be guided to deliverance. 

01:14:24.251 --> 01:14:26.086
Let's burn it right away.

01:14:27.921 --> 01:14:28.964
Okay.

01:14:30.966 --> 01:14:33.168
Let's burn it as soon as dawn breaks.

01:14:33.169 --> 01:14:35.721
Yes, let's do that, it would
lift a weight off my chest!

01:14:35.722 --> 01:14:37.598
For real.

01:14:37.598 --> 01:14:38.557
Excuse me...

01:14:39.141 --> 01:14:42.199
I've boiled some noodles inside,
come in and warm yourselves up.

01:14:42.286 --> 01:14:43.856
Oh, yes. We appreciate it.

01:14:43.929 --> 01:14:45.556
- All right.
- This way.

01:14:45.616 --> 01:14:48.128
Right from the start I had a
bad feeling about that grave.

01:14:48.129 --> 01:14:49.561
That mountain's shape
just stretches on and on...

01:14:49.562 --> 01:14:51.862
Come to think of it,
I haven't eaten all day.

01:14:58.227 --> 01:14:59.077
All right.

01:14:59.164 --> 01:15:00.996
Please, have a drink.

01:15:01.063 --> 01:15:03.094
Thank you.

01:15:03.160 --> 01:15:05.459
Thank you, I will enjoy it.

01:15:05.566 --> 01:15:07.273
Here's to everyone's good health!

01:15:07.500 --> 01:15:09.129
The scent is unmatched!

01:15:11.170 --> 01:15:13.947
This is a treasure of a drink.

01:15:13.948 --> 01:15:17.438
- Let me pour you a glass, Venerable.
- This is boiling hot.

01:15:17.524 --> 01:15:18.871
- Yes.
- I'll pour you a drink.

01:15:18.944 --> 01:15:23.276
Do you also have some acorn jelly?
Just kidding, I was trying to be funny.

01:15:24.762 --> 01:15:29.702
CHAPTER V: GHOSTLY FIRE
(ONI)

01:15:31.888 --> 01:15:33.671
Yes, Murayama Junji.

01:15:33.944 --> 01:15:35.280
Don't you remember?

01:15:35.418 --> 01:15:38.325
Our teacher used to mention it
from time to time.

01:15:38.492 --> 01:15:40.196
In Japan... What was it called...

01:15:40.197 --> 01:15:44.539
- A yin-yang master known as The Fox.
- I remember.

01:15:45.064 --> 01:15:46.872
The yin-yang master, Murayama.

01:15:46.959 --> 01:15:49.628
Teacher said he even met
him once, a long time ago.

01:15:49.775 --> 01:15:52.689
He said his spiritual energy was so
overwhelming that he wasn't a human being.

01:15:52.690 --> 01:15:54.986
That he was, in fact, a fox cub.

01:15:54.987 --> 01:15:56.120
But why do you ask?

01:15:56.200 --> 01:15:57.135
Where are you now?

01:15:57.267 --> 01:15:58.845
Nevermind.

01:15:59.096 --> 01:16:00.222
All right.

01:16:00.589 --> 01:16:02.391
Thank you, Gwangshim.

01:16:02.933 --> 01:16:04.476
Talk to you soon.

01:16:11.110 --> 01:16:12.442
Grandma.

01:16:13.873 --> 01:16:15.279
Grandma.

01:16:19.897 --> 01:16:21.994
I feel strange.

01:17:19.855 --> 01:17:21.553
He took my liver.

01:17:21.659 --> 01:17:22.660
My liver...

01:17:22.906 --> 01:17:24.074
My liver...

01:17:28.746 --> 01:17:30.854
He took my liver.

01:17:30.922 --> 01:17:32.731
Some bastard took my liver.

01:17:32.808 --> 01:17:34.361
The bastard took my liver.

01:17:34.455 --> 01:17:35.641
He took my liver.

01:17:35.714 --> 01:17:37.027
He took my liver.

01:17:37.121 --> 01:17:38.407
He took my liver.

01:17:38.474 --> 01:17:39.358
Where are my clothes?

01:17:39.431 --> 01:17:40.522
Where are my clothes?

01:17:40.589 --> 01:17:42.648
My clothes... my clothes... my clothes...

01:17:42.721 --> 01:17:45.327
- Where are my clothes?
- Shit...

01:17:45.394 --> 01:17:46.598
Some bastard took my liver.

01:17:46.672 --> 01:17:48.330
My clothes... my liver...

01:17:48.392 --> 01:17:49.523
He took my liver.

01:19:42.888 --> 01:19:43.987
Hwarim!

01:19:59.123 --> 01:20:01.088
Damn it.

01:20:09.890 --> 01:20:12.307
Shit, this stench of meat...

01:20:27.594 --> 01:20:30.158
Because of the seal,
it pierced through the ceiling.

01:20:33.508 --> 01:20:35.831
This thing... right now...

01:20:37.916 --> 01:20:40.943
What's the matter, you rascal?
Speak!

01:20:42.713 --> 01:20:44.797
This thing, right now it's...

01:20:44.798 --> 01:20:47.808
I think it's in the pigsty
down the valley.

01:20:48.218 --> 01:20:49.803
Wake everyone up.

01:20:49.923 --> 01:20:51.013
Yes.

01:22:09.002 --> 01:22:11.882
The seal has been broken.

01:22:13.382 --> 01:22:16.622
Are there humans here?

01:22:19.072 --> 01:22:22.942
I've come to retrieve my helmet.

01:22:23.022 --> 01:22:25.162
Are there humans here?

01:22:26.262 --> 01:22:27.472
No.

01:22:28.282 --> 01:22:29.972
There aren't.

01:22:30.202 --> 01:22:32.232
There are no humans here.

01:22:32.352 --> 01:22:37.002
I'm your subordinate.

01:22:38.642 --> 01:22:41.172
Is that so?

01:22:41.172 --> 01:22:42.392
Then,

01:22:42.392 --> 01:22:46.942
did you bring sweetfish or melon?

01:22:49.812 --> 01:22:53.892
Are the words of your Lord
not reaching your ears?

01:22:55.582 --> 01:22:59.082
I've beheaded the enemy commander.

01:23:08.362 --> 01:23:09.352
No...

01:23:09.402 --> 01:23:10.902
No...

01:23:11.362 --> 01:23:15.102
I'll prepare the sweetfish for you.

01:23:41.762 --> 01:23:44.792
You're a human.

01:24:06.123 --> 01:24:07.334
Run.

01:24:07.951 --> 01:24:08.785
Bong-gil.

01:24:43.979 --> 01:24:45.581
Bong-gil...

01:25:06.182 --> 01:25:07.982
A pagoda.

01:27:18.025 --> 01:27:19.192
Bong-gil...

01:27:19.192 --> 01:27:20.402
Bong-gil.

01:27:20.986 --> 01:27:22.779
Bong-gil! Bong-gil!

01:27:22.779 --> 01:27:23.739
Wake up!

01:27:26.199 --> 01:27:29.494
700,000 won to Kim Young-ja
from the Sunsine Tea House...

01:27:30.037 --> 01:27:32.080
170,000 won at the electronic
appliance store...

01:27:32.080 --> 01:27:34.609
I have to pay 2 million won to the
Thousand Days funeral service company...

01:27:34.683 --> 01:27:36.103
Minus 5 million won to the Mirae Asset company...

01:27:36.104 --> 01:27:38.253
Professor, help me!

01:27:38.672 --> 01:27:40.464
Help me!

01:27:42.007 --> 01:27:44.009
Help me!

01:27:44.099 --> 01:27:45.969
Help me...

01:27:45.969 --> 01:27:47.763
Bong-gil, wake up!

01:27:47.763 --> 01:27:49.681
Try to wake up, Bong-gil...

01:28:02.319 --> 01:28:03.987
This morning in Goseong County, Gangwon Province,

01:28:03.987 --> 01:28:05.697
wild bear attacks resulted in casualties...

01:28:05.697 --> 01:28:09.159
The fever still hasn't subsided, so
I will administer a fever reducer.

01:28:09.159 --> 01:28:10.953
 At the damaged livestock barn in the village, 

01:28:10.953 --> 01:28:14.373
 dozens of pigs were found
with their abdomens torn open, 

01:28:14.373 --> 01:28:18.377
 and two additional bodies were discovered
having suffered the same attack. 

01:28:18.377 --> 01:28:20.337
The victims are a monk from a nearby temple,

01:28:20.337 --> 01:28:23.632
and a migrant worker employed
at the livestock barn.

01:28:23.632 --> 01:28:26.576
 Officials from the county office stated
that the local government and military units 

01:28:26.577 --> 01:28:28.679
 are working together to
track down the wild bears. 

01:28:58.250 --> 01:28:59.793
Forgive me.

01:29:00.925 --> 01:29:03.672
I shouldn't have suggested
pulling him out of there...

01:29:04.673 --> 01:29:06.466
Because of that, Bong-gil...

01:29:08.468 --> 01:29:10.470
And the monk...

01:29:12.173 --> 01:29:17.068
Bong-gil underwent the spiritual affliction
when he was a baseball player and had to quit.

01:29:18.713 --> 01:29:22.015
When he came looking for a teacher
after being abandoned by his family,

01:29:22.572 --> 01:29:25.152
I tried my best to stop him
from becoming a shaman,

01:29:27.454 --> 01:29:29.613
but he said he would be fine
as long as he is with me.

01:29:29.614 --> 01:29:32.826
That he had nothing to fear.

01:29:41.007 --> 01:29:44.062
I was frozen with fear
and I couldn't do anything.

01:29:51.803 --> 01:29:53.388
It left footprints.

01:29:54.149 --> 01:29:56.016
And it had a shadow.

01:29:56.838 --> 01:30:00.078
In shamanism, there's this
widely accepted theory.

01:30:01.024 --> 01:30:06.025
Given that the spirit is incomplete
and lacks a physical form,

01:30:06.026 --> 01:30:12.012
ultimately the body and mind of a
healthy person can never be defeated.

01:30:13.039 --> 01:30:17.286
But that thing... is of a
very different nature.

01:30:17.287 --> 01:30:21.366
It's not just any spirit, but
one bound to an object.

01:30:22.042 --> 01:30:23.009
Bound to an object?

01:30:23.010 --> 01:30:28.039
It emerges when the spirit becomes attached
to an object and they evolve in tandem.

01:30:29.336 --> 01:30:32.219
It's something that should
never exist in our country.

01:30:35.777 --> 01:30:38.225
I couldn't feel anything.

01:30:39.142 --> 01:30:41.011
Neither its identity,

01:30:41.012 --> 01:30:43.166
nor where it came from,

01:30:43.167 --> 01:30:45.899
nor the reason why it dwelled
at the Park family's grave.

01:30:51.196 --> 01:30:53.907
He has many injuries
in the abdominal area.

01:30:54.241 --> 01:30:55.993
He also lost a lot of blood.

01:30:56.368 --> 01:31:00.037
The problem is that his
spine was also affected,

01:31:00.038 --> 01:31:02.291
so let's send him to a larger
hospital right away.

01:31:03.166 --> 01:31:05.794
Since the injuries were caused
by wild animals...

01:31:11.394 --> 01:31:14.997
THE BACKBONE OF THE KOREAN PENINSULA
(BAEKDU-DAEGAN MOUNTAIN RANGE)

01:31:14.998 --> 01:31:17.764
The fox has broken the tiger's spine. 

01:31:38.618 --> 01:31:40.224
 Grave robbers were rampant in those days, 

01:31:40.304 --> 01:31:42.312
 so a modest grave was set up for him
in a place unknown to anyone. 

01:31:42.313 --> 01:31:47.085
 The grave robbers' belongings are still in the storage. 

01:32:16.694 --> 01:32:19.868
"Our land, my comrades".

01:32:19.949 --> 01:32:21.161
"Iron Blood Legion"?

01:32:27.417 --> 01:32:30.170
We've managed to prevent organ damage
in a timely manner.

01:32:30.587 --> 01:32:33.652
We will have to conduct
some additional tests,

01:32:33.653 --> 01:32:37.134
but for now, he should have
regained consciousness...

01:32:37.135 --> 01:32:38.804
It's strange.

01:32:39.137 --> 01:32:41.640
What happened to him?

01:32:41.640 --> 01:32:44.077
Fortunately, he's gotten
past the critical point,

01:32:44.078 --> 01:32:45.936
but they said his spine was affected.

01:32:45.936 --> 01:32:47.145
Can he walk?

01:32:47.145 --> 01:32:48.822
He needs to pull through this.

01:32:48.823 --> 01:32:50.690
Nonetheless, he's healthy.

01:32:52.192 --> 01:32:54.271
What in the world have you
been doing lately?

01:32:54.272 --> 01:32:55.654
Tell me.

01:32:56.683 --> 01:32:58.448
- Gwangshim.
- Yes.

01:32:58.586 --> 01:33:00.617
He reeks of meat.

01:33:03.256 --> 01:33:05.581
I know, that's why I called you.

01:33:06.004 --> 01:33:09.072
How about we play goblins again?
It's been ages.

01:33:10.073 --> 01:33:11.875
Park Ja-hye, what are you waiting for?

01:33:11.876 --> 01:33:12.963
Lock the door.

01:33:12.992 --> 01:33:18.642
CHAPTER VI: IRON STAKE

01:33:22.278 --> 01:33:23.598
Bae Ji-dang.

01:33:23.671 --> 01:33:25.475
Lee Chung-gu.

01:33:25.767 --> 01:33:27.269
Park Gil-ho.

01:33:27.807 --> 01:33:29.183
Shin Pal-gyun.

01:33:31.106 --> 01:33:32.649
Kim Jeong-bok.

01:33:33.107 --> 01:33:35.277
Song Jong-ik.

01:33:35.455 --> 01:33:37.863
Min Geun-ho.

01:33:38.720 --> 01:33:41.825
Jeon Tae-hwan, Im Chung-shin.

01:33:42.868 --> 01:33:44.077
That's right.

01:33:44.578 --> 01:33:48.624
 They look way too determined,
for them to be mere grave robbers. 

01:34:17.098 --> 01:34:20.364
My goodness, ladies! It's been a
while since we've seen each other!

01:34:20.810 --> 01:34:22.013
Is everyone here?

01:34:22.086 --> 01:34:23.742
I arrived just now.

01:34:23.885 --> 01:34:26.396
The harvest season is over
and the cold is creeping in,

01:34:26.397 --> 01:34:28.330
so tell me, is everyone all right?

01:34:28.414 --> 01:34:31.269
Oh my, since we've all gathered like this,

01:34:31.270 --> 01:34:33.488
I should whip up some pancakes
or something to bring over.

01:34:33.489 --> 01:34:35.171
Don't worry.

01:34:35.251 --> 01:34:39.272
I already brought sorghum rice
cakes and some boiled pork.

01:34:39.273 --> 01:34:43.052
I was really wondering where this
delicious smell was coming from...

01:34:43.053 --> 01:34:44.424
I hope you brought enough.

01:34:44.425 --> 01:34:47.057
Yes, she brought plenty!

01:34:47.058 --> 01:34:49.171
Even if we eat our fill,
there will still be some left.

01:34:49.172 --> 01:34:53.160
Then why don't we invite over Mr. Jang from
across the street, and Mr. Je-cheon as well?

01:34:53.161 --> 01:34:55.327
Why bother inviting busy people over?

01:34:55.328 --> 01:34:57.337
Let's just eat quietly
among ourselves.

01:34:57.338 --> 01:34:59.805
That's right, let's just
eat among ourselves.

01:34:59.806 --> 01:35:02.389
Did you also bring some sweetfish?

01:35:07.663 --> 01:35:08.537
What's this?

01:35:08.966 --> 01:35:11.143
I think Mr. Yoon has arrived!

01:35:11.144 --> 01:35:13.000
What are you talking about?

01:35:13.130 --> 01:35:14.853
Haven't you heard that Mr. Yoon
is working late tonight?

01:35:14.854 --> 01:35:18.463
That's right, there's no way
Mr. Yoon could have come.

01:35:18.463 --> 01:35:20.232
What is everyone talking about?

01:35:20.233 --> 01:35:21.377
Just tell us already!

01:35:21.464 --> 01:35:23.218
Don't talk to him.

01:35:23.885 --> 01:35:27.027
I heard he had an encounter with
something extremely dangerous.

01:35:27.028 --> 01:35:31.312
How dangerous could it have been,
to have him bedridden like this?

01:35:31.405 --> 01:35:32.311
Haven't you heard?

01:35:33.584 --> 01:35:36.648
They say he met a spiritual
guest last night.

01:35:37.772 --> 01:35:40.552
What nonsense are you even spouting?

01:35:41.399 --> 01:35:43.905
Goodness gracious... Mr. Yoon?!

01:35:44.122 --> 01:35:47.074
What did you see that's
got you scared stiff in bed?

01:35:47.781 --> 01:35:49.127
No way!

01:35:49.128 --> 01:35:52.021
This guy looks completely healthy to me.

01:35:52.456 --> 01:35:54.124
Who was it?

01:35:54.875 --> 01:35:57.294
The spiritual guest you met.

01:35:57.753 --> 01:35:59.338
Tell me already.

01:36:02.049 --> 01:36:05.093
My master.

01:36:06.252 --> 01:36:07.638
Your master?

01:36:08.388 --> 01:36:09.723
What kind of master?

01:36:16.448 --> 01:36:19.524
Speak, you scoundrel.

01:36:26.792 --> 01:36:32.352
My master killed 10,000 people
and became a divine entity.

01:36:36.672 --> 01:36:38.692
That master of yours...

01:36:39.902 --> 01:36:42.472
Where is he now?

01:37:02.842 --> 01:37:06.182
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:37:06.422 --> 01:37:10.312
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:37:10.552 --> 01:37:14.002
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:37:16.118 --> 01:37:17.457
Cherry blossoms...

01:37:18.982 --> 01:37:24.362
He is the general who guards that place.

01:37:39.989 --> 01:37:41.440
What the hell?

01:37:44.362 --> 01:37:45.552
Master!

01:37:45.552 --> 01:37:47.722
Grace me with your attention!

01:37:47.742 --> 01:37:50.082
Here I am,

01:37:50.132 --> 01:37:53.892
willing to serve as your vessel!

01:38:07.011 --> 01:38:09.927
I'll wrench that piece of flesh from you.

01:38:11.519 --> 01:38:12.804
Ja-hye...

01:38:13.597 --> 01:38:15.265
Come here.

01:38:15.724 --> 01:38:17.643
Please, save me, Ja-hye...

01:38:23.903 --> 01:38:26.443
Filthy whores.

01:38:26.556 --> 01:38:28.307
You will all die.

01:38:42.091 --> 01:38:43.884
Hwarim, stay out of this.

01:38:43.964 --> 01:38:45.304
It's a Japanese ghost.

01:38:45.378 --> 01:38:46.713
I know.

01:38:46.796 --> 01:38:49.357
These spirits will kill you even if
you have no connections to them.

01:38:49.358 --> 01:38:52.135
They kill anyone who merely approaches.

01:38:52.970 --> 01:38:55.012
Haven't you seen it with your
own eyes in Japan, back then?

01:38:55.013 --> 01:38:57.182
Don't go even near them!

01:38:58.475 --> 01:39:00.811
Even if your grandmother is by your side,

01:39:01.728 --> 01:39:03.455
you mustn't get involved.

01:39:03.511 --> 01:39:04.731
Let's go, Ja-hye.

01:39:05.023 --> 01:39:06.524
Then what about Bong-gil?

01:39:09.653 --> 01:39:10.779
I'll give you a call.

01:39:10.882 --> 01:39:11.655
Let's go.

01:39:26.990 --> 01:39:28.922
Is that thing down there?

01:39:30.549 --> 01:39:33.218
That means it has returned
to its original place.

01:39:34.011 --> 01:39:35.971
But why did you go back there?

01:39:35.971 --> 01:39:36.638
Well?

01:39:37.859 --> 01:39:38.724
Well?!

01:39:38.859 --> 01:39:41.727
Park Ji-yong said something
before he died.

01:39:43.228 --> 01:39:45.564
"The fox has broken the tiger's spine."

01:39:47.149 --> 01:39:49.276
What does that mean?

01:39:49.484 --> 01:39:51.648
In feng shui,

01:39:51.649 --> 01:39:54.822
our country is seen as having
the shape of a tiger.

01:39:54.823 --> 01:39:56.950
A tiger holding the continent in its grip.

01:39:57.284 --> 01:39:58.076
So?

01:39:58.172 --> 01:40:00.548
The numbers engraved on the
back of that gravestone.

01:40:00.628 --> 01:40:02.164
Latitude and longitude!

01:40:02.263 --> 01:40:03.767
Where do you think that place is?

01:40:03.768 --> 01:40:05.835
Exactly, right there.

01:40:05.836 --> 01:40:07.979
Right atop the tiger's spine.

01:40:07.980 --> 01:40:11.047
That yin-yang master known as The Fox,
whom Hwarim mentioned...

01:40:11.590 --> 01:40:13.425
That fox cub...

01:40:14.593 --> 01:40:16.261
He went there, and...

01:40:16.595 --> 01:40:19.264
Drove an iron stake into the ground.

01:40:23.834 --> 01:40:26.188
Then why was the Park family's
grave on top of it?

01:40:28.536 --> 01:40:30.645
These determined-looking people

01:40:30.646 --> 01:40:33.052
were constantly searching for and
extracting such stakes from the ground,

01:40:33.053 --> 01:40:35.855
so he covered it with the grave of a
high-ranking official from that era,

01:40:35.856 --> 01:40:37.258
to prevent anyone from approaching it.

01:40:37.259 --> 01:40:38.158
Then...

01:40:38.158 --> 01:40:40.618
Why does a spirit dwell there?

01:40:40.786 --> 01:40:41.787
Well?

01:40:44.302 --> 01:40:47.322
 He is the general who guards that place. 

01:40:47.352 --> 01:40:49.512
 My master. 

01:40:54.262 --> 01:40:58.292
 38.3417° - 128.3189° 

01:40:58.849 --> 01:41:00.055
Perhaps...

01:41:01.014 --> 01:41:03.100
He's there to protect that iron stake.

01:41:17.805 --> 01:41:19.085
Lee Hwarim...

01:41:19.152 --> 01:41:22.202
Though we have a business relationship,

01:41:23.036 --> 01:41:25.219
- let me ask you a favor that won't cost a thing.
- Hold on.

01:41:25.299 --> 01:41:27.395
If you're harboring some absurd ideas,
don't even mention them.

01:41:27.396 --> 01:41:28.469
So they crushed the national spirit

01:41:28.470 --> 01:41:31.180
and split the country by driving
iron stakes into the ground?

01:41:31.181 --> 01:41:32.696
Do you still believe in these things?

01:41:32.783 --> 01:41:35.257
Those iron stakes at the temple are all for land surveying!

01:41:35.309 --> 01:41:36.675
You know that too!

01:41:36.822 --> 01:41:39.636
Even the academic conferences have
stated that 99% of them are fakes.

01:41:39.709 --> 01:41:41.377
And the remaining 1%?

01:41:42.681 --> 01:41:44.975
- Elder Go.
- What is it?

01:41:45.095 --> 01:41:47.060
This isn't just an ordinary grave.

01:41:47.194 --> 01:41:49.479
There's something meticulously
calculated about it!

01:41:51.178 --> 01:41:54.669
Not long ago, you witnessed people
dying because of that grave.

01:41:54.670 --> 01:41:56.671
Do you want to see that happen again?

01:41:56.672 --> 01:41:57.613
Sang-deok.

01:41:57.613 --> 01:41:59.658
Regardless of where that
iron stake was driven,

01:41:59.659 --> 01:42:02.982
we've lived just fine until now,
without any issues!

01:42:02.983 --> 01:42:04.661
So what's gotten into you all of a sudden?

01:42:04.766 --> 01:42:05.829
That's right.

01:42:06.496 --> 01:42:07.998
You and I,

01:42:08.192 --> 01:42:12.292
we sold land to wealthy people
and have lived well from it since.

01:42:12.293 --> 01:42:13.669
And that's exactly why!

01:42:13.670 --> 01:42:16.089
Elder Go, it's land we're
talking about here, land!

01:42:17.495 --> 01:42:20.927
The very land our future grandchildren
will tread upon and live their lives!

01:42:20.928 --> 01:42:23.597
And you, and I, and all of us!

01:42:23.843 --> 01:42:25.933
And those who come after us.

01:42:29.311 --> 01:42:31.731
Hwarim, you said it's a spirit
bound to an object.

01:42:31.732 --> 01:42:34.302
If that spirit is indeed
bound to the iron stake,

01:42:34.303 --> 01:42:36.754
doesn't it mean we simply
need to remove the stake?

01:42:36.818 --> 01:42:40.197
And once we get rid of that stake,
Bong-gil might also get better!

01:42:43.867 --> 01:42:44.952
Gosh...

01:42:45.410 --> 01:42:49.430
But you said the general, or
whatever it is, is clinging to it!

01:42:49.510 --> 01:42:51.250
So how are we going to pull it out?

01:42:51.415 --> 01:42:53.085
You've seen that thing at the temple, too.

01:42:53.085 --> 01:42:54.795
The mere thought...

01:42:55.921 --> 01:42:58.048
 Lure it like a beast, 

01:43:00.217 --> 01:43:02.511
 and speak to the spirit. 

01:43:04.855 --> 01:43:07.057
 Do you really believe we can do this? 

01:43:07.166 --> 01:43:08.682
Some things are within our power,

01:43:08.683 --> 01:43:11.561
- while some aren't!
- I'm sorry, but that spirit...

01:43:12.156 --> 01:43:14.372
It's not something we can get rid of.

01:43:14.830 --> 01:43:16.816
Even if it doesn't hold grudges,

01:43:16.817 --> 01:43:19.280
it kills everyone who approaches it.

01:43:19.361 --> 01:43:21.029
It's a Japanese ghost.

01:43:22.433 --> 01:43:23.573
But...

01:43:23.686 --> 01:43:25.742
Although we can't get rid of it,

01:43:28.452 --> 01:43:30.638
I can make it come out
for a short while.

01:43:31.707 --> 01:43:34.350
I can buy us some time.

01:43:42.990 --> 01:43:44.219
Bong-gil!

01:43:47.241 --> 01:43:49.600
I need more betadine, please.

01:43:49.770 --> 01:43:52.352
I'll sterilize the area again with saline
solution before applying the bandage.

01:43:52.353 --> 01:43:53.353
All right.

01:43:54.021 --> 01:43:55.314
Hold on a second.

01:44:00.402 --> 01:44:02.987
That bastard avoided the tattoos!?

01:44:03.530 --> 01:44:05.198
What kind of tattoo is this?

01:44:06.408 --> 01:44:08.076
A scripture to ward off evil spirits.

01:44:32.928 --> 01:44:34.603
Excuse me.

01:44:35.020 --> 01:44:38.065
There have been victims in the
vicinity due to wild animals, so...

01:44:40.233 --> 01:44:42.319
Oh, I...

01:44:42.569 --> 01:44:44.279
Where...

01:44:44.655 --> 01:44:46.907
Where are you heading to?

01:44:47.042 --> 01:44:48.992
Oh... Well...

01:44:49.530 --> 01:44:52.746
We’ve come to tidy up
the gravesite up there.

01:44:52.858 --> 01:44:53.984
Ah, yes...

01:44:54.122 --> 01:44:58.293
We've been searching that mountain with
the military for the past few days.

01:44:58.352 --> 01:44:59.747
Oh, we...

01:44:59.847 --> 01:45:01.463
We'll head up there right away,

01:45:01.533 --> 01:45:03.215
and return as soon as the job is done.

01:45:03.274 --> 01:45:04.424
Oh, I see...

01:45:04.716 --> 01:45:05.676
Clear the way for them.

01:46:02.649 --> 01:46:05.213
We're heading back.
Returning to base.

01:46:05.214 --> 01:46:06.839
Since we've given him
what he wanted,

01:46:06.840 --> 01:46:09.489
he'll likely make a move
at around 2 o'clock.

01:46:09.945 --> 01:46:12.701
If I can lure him to the yew tree,

01:46:12.816 --> 01:46:15.370
I'll buy us as much time as possible.

01:46:15.871 --> 01:46:18.582
We'll pull out the iron stake right away,

01:46:18.749 --> 01:46:21.043
so hang in there for just 30 minutes.

01:46:21.188 --> 01:46:22.294
And you two...

01:46:22.295 --> 01:46:23.545
After you pull out the iron stake,

01:46:26.581 --> 01:46:30.168
I'll cleanse it with this horse
blood, then I'll dispose of it.

01:46:31.678 --> 01:46:32.888
Professor Kim.

01:46:33.722 --> 01:46:35.432
That iron stake...

01:46:36.642 --> 01:46:38.468
Are you sure it's there?

01:46:41.647 --> 01:46:43.273
One hundred percent.

01:46:51.160 --> 01:46:52.074
Gwangshim.

01:46:52.185 --> 01:46:54.076
Please look after Bong-gil today.

01:46:54.226 --> 01:46:56.870
If things go south,
he will be in danger.

01:47:18.141 --> 01:47:19.351
Stop staring.

01:47:19.905 --> 01:47:21.770
She said he'll come out
at around 2 o'clock.

01:47:34.491 --> 01:47:35.826
Elder Go.

01:47:36.243 --> 01:47:39.041
In any case, thank you
for accompanying me.

01:47:39.127 --> 01:47:40.737
"Though one may be overpowered,

01:47:40.811 --> 01:47:43.292
two can defend themselves,

01:47:43.453 --> 01:47:45.946
for a cord of three strands
is not quickly broken."

01:47:46.737 --> 01:47:49.038
Ecclesiastes 4:12.

01:47:51.174 --> 01:47:52.259
Amen.

01:48:09.527 --> 01:48:10.694
Gwangshim.

01:48:11.790 --> 01:48:13.728
I hope we won't have to sacrifice it.

01:48:15.282 --> 01:48:17.659
It will die in Bong-gil's place.

01:48:19.494 --> 01:48:23.556
But you love eating fried chicken
at Kyochon, so what's the issue?

01:51:24.032 --> 01:51:27.432
Have you eaten your fill?

01:51:43.740 --> 01:51:44.950
This side.

01:51:57.122 --> 01:52:00.382
May I ask who's there?

01:52:04.452 --> 01:52:08.302
My mountain is disturbed.

01:52:11.582 --> 01:52:16.162
Is this your mountain?

01:52:17.752 --> 01:52:21.100
That's exactly so.
This is my mountain.

01:52:21.872 --> 01:52:25.892
What's the deal with
this damned old tree?

01:52:25.922 --> 01:52:30.982
But why don't I hear gunshots
or the clash of swords?

01:52:31.032 --> 01:52:33.472
Those are things of the past.

01:52:34.032 --> 01:52:35.882
The war is long over.

01:52:35.892 --> 01:52:37.632
No!

01:52:37.652 --> 01:52:41.902
Our war is not yet over!

01:52:52.752 --> 01:52:57.322
What binds you to this place?

01:52:59.492 --> 01:53:04.922
Originally, I was enshrined
at the Daitoku Temple,

01:53:04.982 --> 01:53:10.302
but that cunning fox, instead of taking me
to the Namsan Shrine, he brought me here!

01:53:11.782 --> 01:53:14.692
Gatahito's sons must have
ordered him to do so.

01:53:14.722 --> 01:53:17.972
Or maybe it was Makoto's doing...

01:53:26.292 --> 01:53:28.862
This is now a peaceful land.

01:53:28.872 --> 01:53:31.542
You have no reason to be here anymore.

01:53:34.802 --> 01:53:35.902
You're wrong.

01:53:35.962 --> 01:53:37.662
You're wrong!

01:53:37.662 --> 01:53:41.402
We must keep heading north.

01:53:41.402 --> 01:53:44.532
Lift your silver guns and swords
and keep moving forward!

01:53:44.552 --> 01:53:45.562
To the north.

01:53:45.662 --> 01:53:47.042
To the north!

01:53:47.092 --> 01:53:52.162
The valiant centipede knows not of retreat!

01:53:59.216 --> 01:54:00.168
What is this?

01:54:00.419 --> 01:54:02.004
Nothing turns up.

01:54:02.078 --> 01:54:03.797
Damn it.

01:54:07.002 --> 01:54:09.502
As the owner of this domain,
I shall ask again.

01:54:10.242 --> 01:54:12.712
How long have you been here?

01:54:13.712 --> 01:54:17.022
Show proper courtesy!

01:54:17.032 --> 01:54:21.342
I am the one to be feared.

01:54:21.352 --> 01:54:22.952
This is my domain!

01:54:22.952 --> 01:54:26.072
I shall ask again!
What exactly are you?

01:54:32.672 --> 01:54:33.966
There's nothing here.

01:54:33.967 --> 01:54:35.329
Nothing!

01:54:37.100 --> 01:54:38.149
There's nothing here!

01:54:38.150 --> 01:54:40.291
You said you were one
hundred percent sure!

01:54:47.988 --> 01:54:49.301
Shit!

01:54:49.381 --> 01:54:50.594
Damn it!

01:54:51.042 --> 01:54:53.062
Heed my words.

01:54:54.192 --> 01:55:00.882
Though the enemy beheaded me at Sekigahara,
I've already conquered my physical form.

01:55:00.952 --> 01:55:03.702
I am the God of War!

01:55:03.702 --> 01:55:08.742
He is the eternal master who
never decays, the blazing sword!

01:55:08.743 --> 01:55:11.982
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:55:12.312 --> 01:55:19.032
That fox put a spell on me,
I must guard this place!

01:55:30.422 --> 01:55:33.752
Have you taken command of someone?

01:55:35.122 --> 01:55:39.512
Set free the human you're controlling!

01:55:39.512 --> 01:55:41.242
Hurry!

01:55:41.312 --> 01:55:42.942
Please!

01:55:51.812 --> 01:55:53.672
A human!

01:55:54.312 --> 01:55:56.052
March forth!

01:55:56.982 --> 01:55:58.802
March forth!

01:55:59.512 --> 01:56:01.172
March forth!

01:56:03.042 --> 01:56:04.692
March forth!

01:56:14.702 --> 01:56:17.332
That old hag!

01:56:47.628 --> 01:56:49.379
- Have you found it?
- No.

01:56:49.379 --> 01:56:51.006
- There's nothing there!
- What do you mean?

01:56:51.006 --> 01:56:52.060
There's nothing there!

01:56:52.133 --> 01:56:53.300
We must leave right away!

01:57:10.465 --> 01:57:11.568
Sang-deok.

01:57:14.988 --> 01:57:16.323
It's not possible.

01:57:16.442 --> 01:57:17.783
It's not possible!

01:57:30.322 --> 01:57:33.542
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:57:33.562 --> 01:57:37.072
Please return, my Lord!

01:57:37.112 --> 01:57:41.232
38.3417° - 128.3189°

01:57:41.265 --> 01:57:43.225
Kim Sang-deok!

01:57:55.787 --> 01:57:56.611
Sang-deok!

01:57:56.863 --> 01:57:58.323
Get out of there quickly!

01:58:11.926 --> 01:58:13.898
 Then why does a spirit dwell there? 

01:58:13.985 --> 01:58:15.844
 He said he's the general who guards that place. 

01:58:15.930 --> 01:58:17.771
 That means it has returned
to its original place. 

01:58:17.831 --> 01:58:19.970
 Have you ever seen a coffin
standing vertically? 

01:58:24.162 --> 01:58:25.517
 It's fire. 

01:58:26.476 --> 01:58:29.521
 That fire goes into the earth. 

01:58:30.606 --> 01:58:31.565
Get out of there!

01:58:47.062 --> 01:58:49.072
Will you become my subordinate?

01:58:51.442 --> 01:58:53.272
If not...

01:58:53.972 --> 01:58:56.952
Will you offer me your liver?

01:59:00.682 --> 01:59:05.622
I memorized the full text of the
Diamond Sutra inscribed on your body.

01:59:06.322 --> 01:59:08.182
It's been over 500 years!

01:59:11.256 --> 01:59:13.273
The iron stuck in the ground...

01:59:14.650 --> 01:59:16.902
And the fire protecting that place.

01:59:17.992 --> 01:59:19.902
The liver...

01:59:20.902 --> 01:59:23.462
Please consume it!

01:59:23.472 --> 01:59:25.512
That fresh liver...

01:59:31.917 --> 01:59:33.410
Horse blood! The horse blood!

01:59:47.422 --> 01:59:49.272
White horse blood...

01:59:50.882 --> 01:59:52.072
It burns!

01:59:57.702 --> 02:00:00.182
Please get back inside, my Lord!

02:00:00.282 --> 02:00:04.132
You mustn't get caught again.

02:00:07.160 --> 02:00:09.435
 It's a spirit bound to an object. 

02:00:09.436 --> 02:00:13.834
 The spirit becomes attached to an
object and they evolve in tandem. 

02:00:16.962 --> 02:00:18.046
That's right.

02:00:18.463 --> 02:00:19.881
It's iron.

02:00:21.527 --> 02:00:25.137
You yourself are the burning iron.

02:00:31.393 --> 02:00:32.477
Sang-deok!

02:00:32.769 --> 02:00:34.563
- Sang-deok!
- Wake up!

02:00:34.641 --> 02:00:36.389
Lift him onto your back,
we have to leave right away.

02:01:35.290 --> 02:01:36.959
It's earth...

02:01:39.044 --> 02:01:41.221
And the tree's wood.

02:01:41.838 --> 02:01:46.783
Above the earth's energy, the elements
of fire, water, wood and metal...

02:01:46.784 --> 02:01:49.028
They complete the cycle
of the four seasons.

02:01:53.684 --> 02:01:57.019
Fire and water are polar opposites.

02:01:57.020 --> 02:01:59.898
Metal and wood are also polar opposites.

02:02:08.615 --> 02:02:09.783
It's done!

02:02:28.594 --> 02:02:31.179
Burning metal...

02:02:32.806 --> 02:02:35.066
Its polar opposite is...

02:02:35.892 --> 02:02:37.978
Soaked wood.

02:02:48.113 --> 02:02:50.957
Water quenches fire...

02:02:58.665 --> 02:03:00.300
And the soaked wood...

02:03:02.961 --> 02:03:05.055
...withstands the metal!

02:03:20.553 --> 02:03:21.730
Gwangshim, wait a minute!

02:03:22.830 --> 02:03:24.057
The blood is black.

02:03:45.921 --> 02:03:48.757
Now... for the last...

02:04:33.677 --> 02:04:34.720
Bong-gil, are you all right?

02:04:42.728 --> 02:04:44.313
Sang-deok...

02:04:44.313 --> 02:04:46.148
- What should we do...
- Professor...

02:04:46.206 --> 02:04:47.816
What should we do?

02:04:47.816 --> 02:04:49.943
This...

02:04:51.528 --> 02:04:53.622
 I'm on the brink of death. 

02:04:54.114 --> 02:04:56.950
 Fortunately, it doesn't hurt that much. 

02:04:56.950 --> 02:04:58.660
Hey, Kim Sang-deok!

02:04:58.660 --> 02:05:00.120
Stay with us!

02:05:00.120 --> 02:05:03.457
 I have always lived close to death. 

02:05:05.542 --> 02:05:06.543
 That's right. 

02:05:07.002 --> 02:05:10.631
 This time, it's simply my turn. 
- 200 joules.

02:05:13.091 --> 02:05:16.345
 Death means returning to the earth. 

02:05:18.013 --> 02:05:20.432
 Peacefully... 

02:05:21.850 --> 02:05:23.769
 Ah, wait a minute. 

02:05:24.102 --> 02:05:25.661
 My daughter's wedding. 

02:05:25.888 --> 02:05:28.607
 Please, Lord, give him the strength
to get through the surgery. 

02:05:28.833 --> 02:05:31.318
 Embrace him in the precious
blood of our Savior. 

02:05:41.399 --> 02:05:43.772
 Over several days, some
people have passed away, 

02:05:43.773 --> 02:05:45.998
 while others have been
gravely injured. 

02:05:45.999 --> 02:05:48.437
 The surveillance camera footage was obtained
following a tip-off from a village resident... 

02:05:48.438 --> 02:05:50.796
 After a long search, the soldiers 

02:05:50.796 --> 02:05:54.132
 finally managed to capture a wild bear alive. 

02:05:55.092 --> 02:05:59.429
 The deliberation over saving or sacrificing
the innocent bear has sparked a heated debate. 

02:05:59.429 --> 02:06:01.640
 Public opinion is fiercely divided. 

02:06:01.640 --> 02:06:04.685
 Initially, the plan involved sacrificing the
bear to ensure the safety of the residents, but... 

02:06:04.685 --> 02:06:06.311
Oh...

02:06:06.311 --> 02:06:07.271
He's awake.

02:06:09.022 --> 02:06:10.190
Sang-deok!

02:06:10.941 --> 02:06:12.317
Are you feeling better?

02:06:12.317 --> 02:06:13.110
Yes?

02:06:13.110 --> 02:06:17.614
 Fortunately, Professor Kim
recovered quickly for his age. 

02:06:19.116 --> 02:06:21.201
 And Bong-gil... 

02:06:21.618 --> 02:06:22.536
 Well... 

02:06:22.536 --> 02:06:24.629
Oh, we've been busted.

02:06:24.929 --> 02:06:26.707
Are you kidding me?

02:06:27.612 --> 02:06:28.986
This is our food!

02:06:29.073 --> 02:06:31.211
- So you're eating without me?
- Fine, have some.

02:06:31.211 --> 02:06:32.212
I'll grab a slice.

02:06:32.212 --> 02:06:33.942
Gonna enjoy this.

02:06:44.891 --> 02:06:46.893
What is this, a restaurant?

02:06:47.060 --> 02:06:49.062
Do you come here every day just to eat?

02:06:49.062 --> 02:06:50.856
Do you think I eat because I want to?

02:06:50.856 --> 02:06:53.191
They force me to eat!
Because it's delicious.

02:06:53.359 --> 02:06:54.359
It really is.

02:06:54.515 --> 02:06:56.153
He's fasting, can't be helped.

02:06:56.153 --> 02:06:58.413
Well, at least someone's
got to eat to stay alive.

02:06:58.414 --> 02:07:01.524
Sang-deok, take this as an
opportunity to lose some weight.

02:07:07.989 --> 02:07:09.791
 Winter has passed, 

02:07:09.791 --> 02:07:12.085
 and everyone returned to their daily lives. 

02:07:14.671 --> 02:07:15.963
 As if nothing had ever happened. 

02:07:15.964 --> 02:07:17.716
Let's go!

02:07:40.460 --> 02:07:45.619
 In this world, I dwell but briefly 

02:07:45.690 --> 02:07:54.126
 Singing hymns till daylight fades 

02:07:54.127 --> 02:07:56.971
 Should You call me, Lord, I'll answer 

02:07:56.972 --> 02:08:02.219
 Marching forth to glory's shades 

02:08:02.219 --> 02:08:03.808
 Heaven's gates stand wide before me... 

02:08:03.875 --> 02:08:07.165
I clearly told them it needs to be
positioned in alignment with the sun.

02:08:07.166 --> 02:08:10.510
Merely facing it southward does
not make it auspicious by default.

02:08:10.511 --> 02:08:12.361
Then what should we do?

02:08:22.628 --> 02:08:23.699
Next up...

02:08:23.768 --> 02:08:26.815
The groom and bride
will bow to each other.

02:08:26.816 --> 02:08:28.662
The groom and bride will now greet.

02:08:39.433 --> 02:08:42.968
Next up, the family members and close
friends of the bride and groom will gather

02:08:42.968 --> 02:08:44.469
- for the photo session.
- Hey.

02:08:44.469 --> 02:08:46.841
- Elder Go!
- Please come forward.

02:08:46.842 --> 02:08:48.098
Hey, come here.

02:08:48.965 --> 02:08:51.977
Why would we squeeze in with
the close relatives? Forget it!

02:08:54.688 --> 02:08:56.398
Let's just take one photo.

02:08:56.398 --> 02:08:58.025
Let's go and take just one photo.

02:08:58.067 --> 02:09:01.486
- We're like family at this point.
- But it's a family photograph...

02:09:04.478 --> 02:09:06.116
The tall person in the middle,

02:09:06.116 --> 02:09:07.951
please step back a bit.

02:09:07.951 --> 02:09:09.661
The person on the left wearing glasses,

02:09:09.661 --> 02:09:11.246
please move in a little closer.

02:09:11.246 --> 02:09:12.205
Yes.

02:09:12.923 --> 02:09:15.575
Both the father and the daughter
sporting bellies...

02:09:15.576 --> 02:09:17.934
What on earth is this?
For goodness' sake.

02:09:17.935 --> 02:09:19.421
All right, we'll take the photo.

02:09:20.649 --> 02:09:21.632
Father of the bride...

02:09:21.712 --> 02:09:23.622
Look straight ahead.

02:09:23.689 --> 02:09:25.844
Yes, thank you all for your patience.

02:09:26.654 --> 02:09:28.221
Now, everyone, smile together.

02:09:29.222 --> 02:09:32.225
One, two, three!

02:09:32.226 --> 02:09:35.226
EXHUMA

02:09:38.628 --> 02:09:42.122
Choi Min-sik

02:09:44.129 --> 02:09:47.423
Kim Go-eun

02:09:49.025 --> 02:09:51.425
Yoo Hae-jin

02:09:53.228 --> 02:09:55.624
Lee Do-hyun

02:09:57.222 --> 02:09:59.924
Kim Min-jun, Kim Jae-cheol

02:10:01.223 --> 02:10:03.829
Kim Sun-young, Kim Ji-an

02:10:05.125 --> 02:10:07.827
a Jang Jae-hyun film
